window.AKK_FARMING_IMMORTALITY_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_FARMING_IMMORTALITY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Testing Spiritual Roots","paragraphs":["\"Hurry! All children under ten years old in the village, gather at the village entrance right now!\"","A rushed shout carried all the way from the eastern end of the village, startling the sparrows in the trees into fluttering wildly into the air.","\"The immortal sect is here to recruit disciples!\"","The previously quiet Great Tree Village instantly erupted into chaos.","\"An immortal sect? Is that for real?\"","\"Of course it's real! The immortal master is right at the village entrance, and we only have a quarter of an hour—no late admittance. Anyone with little kids should hurry and bring them over, who knows, they might have a predestined fate with cultivation!\"","\"This old man has lived for more than sixty years, and this is the first time I've ever heard of such a thing. Could this be a scam?\"","\"Can a scammer fly down from the sky?\"","Those words immediately silenced all the villagers who still harbored doubts. In just a few moments, the hundred-year-old old pagoda tree at the village entrance was packed full of people.","A dozen still-ignorant children were pushed to the front by their parents, all craning their necks, looking at the blue-robed woman under the tree with a mix of fear and curiosity.","The woman looked no more than twenty years old, her long hair held back only by a single jade hairpin, the hem of her spotless robe completely free of dust. Even though she was standing right in the middle of the crowd, she seemed separated from the surrounding dirt and noise by an invisible barrier.","A slightly bold little boy asked in a soft voice, \"Are you an immortal master?\"","The woman glanced down at him, her expression calm, not haughty in the slightest.","\"I am not an immortal, just a cultivator.\"","The moment her voice fell, she waved her hand, and everyone's vision blurred for a second before a half-human-tall gray-white stone platform appeared out of thin air under the old pagoda tree. A collective gasp rose from the crowd.","Chen Su paid no mind to the crowd's amazement, and simply said, \"Line up, place your hands on the stone platform one by one. We will find out immediately if you have spiritual roots.\"","The adults quickly herded their children into a long line.","The first child stepped forward trembling, placed a hand on the platform, and the stone did not react at all.","Chen Su glanced at them, and said calmly, \"No spiritual root. Next.\"","The second, the third, the fourth.","\"No spiritual root.\"","\"No spiritual root.\"","\"Still no spiritual root.\"","The same words repeated over and over.","The villagers, who had been full of hope at first, gradually fell quiet. Some of the children who had been tested were still confused, while others had already understood they had not been selected, and walked back to their parents with their heads hanging low.","Before long, the last child stepped back, and the stone platform had not lit up with even the tiniest glimmer of light the entire time. Chen Su was not surprised by this—among ordinary mortals, those with spiritual roots were one in ten thousand.","\"Fine then.\"","Chen Su raised her hand, just about to put away the spirit testing platform, when a rush of footsteps suddenly came from the distance.","\"Immortal Master! Wait, Immortal Master!\"","A tall, broad-shouldered man came running from the end of the village path, huffing and puffing, holding two little girls in his arms.","He had run so fast that his forehead was covered in sweat, and the front of his tunic was soaked through, but he did not even bother to catch his breath before speaking urgently, \"Immortal Master, my two daughters were playing by the river earlier, and I wasted time looking for them. Please give them one more chance!\"","Chen Su glanced up at the sky. The quarter of an hour had already passed.","But in the end, she did not refuse, and only said softly, \"Come forward.\"","\"Thank you Immortal Master, thank you so much Immortal Master!\"","Qin Ye thanked her repeatedly, quickly setting his elder daughter down. The two little girls looked nearly seven years old, sharing seven out of ten similar facial features. The older girl was quiet and composed, while the younger one stared at the spirit testing platform with wide round eyes, full of unmasked curiosity.","\"Zhenzhen, you go first.\"","Qin Ye held his elder daughter's hand and led her to the stone platform. Qin Zhen glanced up at Chen Su, then placed her palm on the platform as she was told.","A few moments passed, and the platform did not react at all.","Chen Su said, \"No spiritual root.\"","The light in Qin Ye's eyes dimmed for a second, but Qin Zhen simply pulled her hand back quietly, showing little disappointment, and instead turned to look back at her little sister.","\"Jiajia, it's your turn.\"","\"Okay.\"","Qin Jia leaned out from her father's arms, stretched out her small, fair little hand, and pressed it smack onto the stone platform.","\"It's cool.\"","The second her words ended, the stone platform shook violently. Chen Su's originally calm expression changed drastically, and in the next instant, a dazzling white light shot straight up into the sky from the platform! A biting cold spread out in all directions, and the noisy village entrance fell completely silent in the blink of an eye.","Chen Su stared intently at the spirit testing platform, her breath catching for a split second. Pure white spiritual light, cold aura seeping out, not a single trace of any other attribute mixed in.","\"A top-grade ice spiritual root!\"","Her usual steady voice carried a clear, obvious fluctuation for the very first time. To make sure she had not misread it, Chen Su poured another wisp of spiritual energy into the spirit testing platform.","It really was a top-grade ice spiritual root. Waves of shock surged through Chen Su's mind. The Qingyun Sect had not taken in a disciple with such exceptional talent in nearly a hundred years. As long as this child did not meet an untimely death halfway through her cultivation, she would at least reach the Nascent Soul realm in the future, and might even have a shot at touching the path of Soul Transformation.","She had come down the mountain only to complete a routine sect mission, never expecting to find such a once-in-a-generation unpolished jade in this remote little village.","\"Wonderful, wonderful, wonderful!\"","Chen Su said three \"wonderful\"s in a row, a rare hint of joy appearing in her eyes. She put away the spirit testing platform, squatted down, and did her best to make her voice sound gentle.","\"What is your name?\"","\"My name is Qin Jia.\"","The little girl blinked, then corrected earnestly, \"The Jia that means praise, not the jia that means home.\"","The corners of Chen Su's lips lifted into a faint smile.","\"Qin Jia, would you like to come with me to the Qingyun Sect to practice cultivation?\"","\"What is cultivation?\"","\"Once you cultivate, you can fly on a sword, cast magical spells, and even pull items out of thin air the way I did just now.\"","Qin Jia's eyes lit up instantly.","\"Is that like doing magic tricks?\"","Qin Ye, who was holding her, turned bright red with panic, terrified that his daughter's innocent, childish words had offended the cultivator, but he did not dare to interrupt rashly. Chen Su was not offended at all.","\"Something like that.\"","Qin Jia immediately clapped her hands excitedly. \"I want to learn! I want to learn how to whoosh things out of nowhere!\"","Seeing that more and more villagers were gathering around, and the murmurs of discussion were growing louder, Chen Su frowned slightly.","\"This is not a good place to talk. Take me to your home.\"","Qin Ye nodded hurriedly. \"This way, Immortal Master.\"","The Qin family's home was not far from the village entrance. Before the group had walked even a few steps, most of the villagers in the whole village had followed after them. After all, for such a remote mountain village, an immortal sect recruiting a disciple was a once-in-a-hundred-year event, especially since the one chosen was the Qin family’s younger daughter that everyone knew.","Once they stepped through the Qin family's courtyard gate, Chen Su lifted a finger and tapped gently, and an invisible barrier instantly wrapped around the entire house. The chattering voices of the villagers outside cut off abruptly, leaving Qin Ye both shocked and awed.","Just a moment ago, it had been as noisy as a market outside, but now not even a sliver of sound could get through. Such a feat was completely beyond the comprehension of ordinary mortals.","Before long, all the members of the Qin family had gathered in the main hall. The Qin family did not have a complicated household structure.","The grandfather Qin Huai, grandmother Wang Sumei, the eldest son Qin Ye and his wife Liu Zhen, and the second son Qin Wen. The two little girls Qin Zhen and Qin Jia were each held tight in one of Qin Ye's hands.","Chen Su got straight to the point. \"I am a disciple of the Qingyun Sect. Qin Jia possesses a top-grade ice spiritual root, with exceptional cultivation talent. If she joins our sect, she will be able to walk the great path of eternal life in the future.\"","The Qin family did not fully understand exactly what a top-tier ice spirit root entailed, but they could tell from Chen Su's earlier reaction that such a natural gift was extraordinarily rare.","Qin Ye remained silent for a long time before he spoke hesitantly. \"Immortal Master, Jiajia is only six years old. Could we wait a few more years until she is a bit older before she leaves with you?\"","Liu Zhen's eyes immediately turned red the moment she heard this. Qin Jia was still so young that she would occasionally wake up crying for her mother in the middle of the night. How could she bear to let her daughter go off all alone to a completely strange place?","\"Cultivation must begin at a young age. The Qingyun Sect only accepts children under ten years old, and the younger the child, the easier it is for them to draw qi into their bodies. If this window of opportunity is missed, their path to immortality could be cut off entirely.\"","The room fell completely quiet in an instant.","\"Then maybe she just won't go.\"","Qin Ye spoke out of the blue, leaving everyone stunned, even Chen Su who lifted her eyes slightly in surprise.","Qin Ye held his little daughter tighter in his arms, his voice growing tight with emotion. \"I'm just an unlearned hunter. I don't know anything about the great path of cultivation, nor do I understand the pursuit of immortality and long life. All I know is that she is still too young. She can't bear to leave her parents, and we can't bear to be separated from her either.\"","Liu Zhen could no longer hold back her tears and turned her head to wipe them away. Qin Jia did not understand why the adults had all gone quiet all of a sudden, so she simply reached out and wiped the sweat off her father's forehead.","\"Don't be sad, Daddy.\"","Qin Ye's eyes grew warm with tears.","Chen Su was silent for a moment before speaking slowly. \"If Qin Jia only had an ordinary spirit root, I would not say another word. But a top-tier ice spirit root is extremely rare. If she stays in the mortal world, she will turn to nothing but a handful of loess a hundred years from now. But if she embarks on the path of cultivation, she could live for hundreds of years, or even far longer than that.\"","\"On top of that, she will not be left all alone in the cultivation world. The sect will arrange for her housing, food, clothing, and personal instruction, and she will take a master as her teacher.\"","Qin Huai hesitated for a moment before he could not help but ask, \"Immortal Master, can we go with her together? Jiajia is really too young. Even if only her mother is allowed to stay by her side to take care of her, that would be enough.\"","Chen Su frowned. In the cultivation world, most ordinary families who learned their child possessed such a rare gift would be overjoyed beyond words, rushing to send their child to the immortal sect as soon as possible. This was the first time she had ever come across a family that, faced with such a tremendous opportunity, only cared about their child being too young. But then she thought to herself that the mortal world was after all different from the cultivation world, and her tone softened a little.","\"Mortals are not permitted to enter the cultivation world where the Qingyun Sect resides. The spiritual energy there is so dense that those without spirit roots cannot withstand it with their physical bodies, and anyone who ventures in rashly will end up with their meridians shattering completely.\"","The faces of all the Qin family members turned pale at once.","Chen Su continued, \"However, just outside the cultivation world, there is a city called Neighboring Immortal City that is connected to Qingyun Sect's teleportation array. You can settle down near Neighboring Immortal City. After Qin Jia enters the sect, she can use the sect's teleportation array to travel and meet you once every year.\"","A flicker of emotion crossed Qin Ye's face. Meeting once a year, though still a long stretch of time apart, was far better than never seeing each other for the rest of their lives.","\"Then she will go. Now that there is still a chance for us to meet again, I cannot stand in the way of my daughter's great opportunity,\" Qin Ye said, his throat tight with emotion.","\"I want to go!\"","Qin Jia, who had been standing quietly to the side, spoke up all of a sudden, drawing everyone's gaze to her.","She clearly did not truly understand what parting meant, and said excitedly, \"I want to learn magic tricks from Fairy Sister. Once I learn them all, I will come back and perform for Daddy, for Mommy, for Grandfather and Grandmother, and also for my elder sister!\"","As she spoke, she wriggled about in Qin Ye's arms, nearly slipping right out of his hold.","\"Jiajia, be still.\"","Qin Zhen spoke suddenly, and Qin Jia froze immediately, quickly covering her mouth with both hands, leaving only her big bright eyes darting around. She was fearless of everyone else in the family, but she was just a little afraid of this usually quiet elder sister of hers. Qin Zhen gently patted her father on the arm.","\"Daddy, put me down.\"","Qin Ye did as she said and set her on the ground. Qin Zhen did not look at Chen Su, but turned to her grandfather Qin Huai first.","\"Grandfather, let us all go to Neighboring Immortal City.\"","Qin Huai was slightly taken aback.","\"Our Qin family only moved to Big Tree Village a few years ago. We have no farmland here, no ancestral property at all. Daddy and my uncle are skilled hunters, Grandfather can make fine bows and arrows, and Mommy and Grandmother are good at sewing, mending, and cooking.\"","Though she was still young, she spoke in a clear, orderly manner.","\"If we could make a living in Big Tree Village, we can make a living in Neighboring Immortal City too. If we stay here, my little sister will have to leave all by herself. But if we move to Neighboring Immortal City, she can come see us every year, and our family will never truly be separated.\"","She paused for a moment, then turned to look at Qin Jia. The little girl still had her hand over her mouth, her eyes shining brightly as she looked back at her.","Qin Zhen said softly, \"My little sister has such a precious chance. We should not let her give it up just because we cannot bear to part with her.\"","Chen Su glanced at Qin Zhen. Earlier during the spirit root test, this girl had shown no resentment at all when she learned she had no spirit root of her own. Now that her younger sister had obtained such an extraordinary natural gift, she felt not a hint of jealousy, but had immediately come up with a perfect plan that satisfied everyone.","Such strength of character was even more precious than a spirit root, Chen Su thought to herself with a quiet sigh, it was truly a pity.","Qin Huai did not say a word for a long time after listening to his granddaughter's words, until at last he let out a heavy sigh.","\"Zhenzhen is right.\"","He looked over at his eldest son.","\"Ye'er, we will go with Jiajia.\"","Wang Sumei nodded through her tears. \"Yes, let's go. It's far better than being separated by thousands of miles, never getting to see each other for the rest of our lives.\"","Liu Zhen held Qin Ye's hand. Tears were still rolling down her cheeks, but her tone was firm.","\"We will all go together.\"","Qin Ye looked down at the little daughter in his arms, then over at his elder daughter standing beside him, his eyes filled with nothing but reluctance.","After a long while, he spoke in a hoarse voice. \"All right.\"","\"We will go to Neighboring Immortal City.\"","Qin Jia finally let go of her hand covering her mouth and cheered out loud.","\"Hooray! We're all going together!\"","The heavy, oppressive atmosphere in the main room finally lifted a little with her cheerful cry, and Chen Su quietly let out a breath of relief. Such a top-tier talent had not slipped through her fingers after all. At that moment, Chen Su had no idea that the fate that would be changed by this encounter with immortal opportunity that day would not be limited to Qin Jia alone.","Seeing that the Qin family had made their decision, Chen Su said no more. She swept her hand over her storage bag, and two pale green jade pendants appeared in her palm.","The pendants were shaped like crescent moons, identical in size and pattern. If the two were fitted together, they would form a perfect full moon.","\"This item is called the Concentric Pendants.\"","Chen Su handed one pendant to Qin Jia, then held the other out to Qin Zhen.","\"They were originally low-grade artifacts used by sect disciples to locate their traveling companions. I have made some modifications to them, and inscribed a mutual sensing formation inside.\"","Qin Zhen did not take it right away, but looked up at her and asked earnestly, \"Can they let us find my little sister?\"","\"They can only sense the general distance, not point out the exact location. The farther apart you are, the dimmer the light from the pendants will grow. The closer you are, the brighter the light will shine. Even if you are thousands of miles apart, the light will be almost invisible to the naked eye, but if you calm your mind and focus, you will still be able to see a faint glimmer.\"","Qin Ye could not help but ask, \"What if the light goes out completely?\"","Chen Su fell silent for a brief moment.","\"These pendants have already recognized each of the two girls as their respective masters.\"","\"As long as the other owner of the jade pendant is still alive, there will remain a wisp of light within the jade pendant. If one owner passes away, the light in the other jade pendant will be completely extinguished, and cracks will begin to form on the pendant's body right after.\"","The main hall fell completely silent in an instant, and Liu Zhen subconsciously hugged the little daughter in her arms tighter.","Qin Jia, however, did not grasp the gravity of the situation at all. She only held up her own half of the jade pendant high, and asked excitedly,","\"Then if I put mine together with my sister's, will it turn into a full moon?\"","Chen Su nodded.","\"When they are close enough, the two pendants will draw towards each other. If they are pressed together, they will briefly merge into one whole.\"","Qin Jia immediately leaned out from her father's embrace, and held her jade pendant out to her elder sister.","\"Sister, let's try it!\"","Only then did Qin Zhen take the other half that belonged to her. The moment the two crescent-shaped jade pendants drew near, they both lit up with a pale cyan glow. As the light blended together, the two pendants gently pulled against each other, fitting together seamlessly to form a full round moon, making Qin Jia's eyes sparkle with delight.","\"It really turned into a full moon!\"","Qin Zhen looked down at the round moon formed in her palm, her fingers tightening slightly around it. After a few moments, the two jade pendants separated on their own. Chen Su threaded thin cords through the small holes on each pendant, and fastened them around the two sisters' necks respectively.","\"Keep them close to your bodies, and do not take them off lightly.\"","\"The United Hearts Pendants can only sense distance and life and death. They cannot transmit voices, nor can they shield you from danger, but as long as the light in the pendant remains, you will know that the other person is still safe and sound.\""]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Sisters Reunited","paragraphs":["A full year had slipped by in the blink of an eye.","Over the past twelve months, the Qin family had spent nearly every day on the road. Before Chen Su left, she had left the Qin family a sum of silver and a map leading to the City of Neighboring Immortals. The Qin party had trekked over mountains and crossed rivers, weathered days of nonstop heavy rain, and fended off bandits lying in wait along the paths. Against all odds, they had finally arrived safely.","The City of Neighboring Immortals was the mortal city closest to the cultivation realm, and on occasion, cultivators from immortal sects would come and go through its gates. Most of the residents within its walls were noble lords, aristocrats, and wealthy merchant clans, all drawn there chasing the sliver of a chance at immortal fate. If a family struck that lucky break, they could rise to prominence in a single leap. It was precisely for this reason that every inch of land in the City of Neighboring Immortals was worth its weight in gold.","The entire Qin family stood outside the city gates, watching the constant stream of ornate horse-drawn carriages coming and going through the entryway, and fell quiet for a moment. They had traveled for an entire year, trekking every step of the way, only to realize they could not even afford a foothold inside the city walls.","Qin Huai pondered for a long time, then lifted his gaze to the rolling, lush mountains stretching beyond the city. \"We can't afford to live in the city, so we won't live there,\" he said slowly, leaning on his wooden staff. \"Our Immortal Master only told us to settle down near the City of Neighboring Immortals, she never said we had to live inside its walls. As long as we are close enough that Jiajia can find us when she comes back, it does not matter where we make our home.\"","Qin Ye nodded in agreement. \"Father is right. We were hunters to begin with. We can make a good living relying on the mountains.\"","Qin Huai looked at his two sons. \"Ye, Wen, go into the mountains and find a place suitable for us to settle.\"","\"We know, Father,\" Qin Ye and Qin Wen said in unison.","The two brothers slung their bows over their shoulders, took their firewood knives, and quickly vanished into the forest. The rest of the Qin family stayed behind to rest at the foot of the mountain.","As dusk fell, Qin Ye hurried out of the woods, his tunic hem dotted with dry leaves, but a bright, excited grin on his face. \"Father, I found a spot!\"","Qin Huai stood up immediately. \"What's it like?\"","\"There's a cave halfway up the mountain. It's dry inside, and there's no sign any wild beasts have ever lived there. Little Wen stayed behind to clear the cave entrance, and sent me back to bring all of you there.\"","Wang Sumei nodded repeatedly as she listened. \"There's water nearby, and it keeps out the wind and rain. That's more than good enough.\"","But Qin Huai was still cautious. \"Are there any footprints of ferocious beasts nearby?\"","\"Wen and I checked the whole area. We didn't find any. There are only tracks left by hares and pheasants.\"","\"Then let's go take a look.\"","The whole group picked up their bags and followed Qin Ye up the mountain. After walking for more than half an hour, they finally spotted the cave. A wide, open flat stretch of land lay just outside its mouth.","\"Mother, sister-in-law, you two rest for a little while first.\"","The Qin family did not waste any time, and quickly set to work tidying the place up. Qin Zhen did not laze about either. She carried armfuls of dry firewood thicker than her own arms, running back and forth to help.","\"Starting tomorrow, Ye, Wen and I will build two wooden huts outside the cave,\" Qin Huai said.","Qin Ye added, \"Wen and I can go hunting in the mountains. The City of Neighboring Immortals has a big population, so game meat and furs should sell for a good price. We can save up silver little by little, and life will get better for sure.\"","Wang Sumei smiled warmly. \"When we first arrived at Dashu Village, the place we lived in was worse than this spot. As long as we're all together as a family, we'll never be unable to make ends meet.\"","At the words \"as a family\", Liu Zhen's hand holding a clay bowl paused slightly. A family, she thought, there is still one missing from us.","Qin Zhen slipped her hand inside her collar, gently closing it around the cool jade pendant she wore. \"Grandfather,\" she said.","\"Hmm?\" Qin Huai responded.","\"Will Jiajia know we're here?\"","Qin Huai looked at her and spoke in a soft, gentle voice. \"Our Immortal Master said that when the time is right, Jiajia will come back. She has a matching jade pendant too. As soon as she gets near the City of Neighboring Immortals, the two of you will know, through the pendants.\"","Qin Zhen nodded quietly. \"I understand.\" She did not ask any more questions, but her hand never loosened its grip on the jade pendant.","At that very moment, thousands of miles away in the Qingyun Sect, the night was deep. A peak covered in snow all year round jutted up above a sea of clouds.","By the side of the frozen lake at the top of the peak, a little girl in a bright red disciple robe sat cross-legged in meditation. Her fair, soft little face was flushed pink from the biting cold. Her eyes were closed, and her hands rested neatly on her knees. But after only a short while, her eyelashes fluttered furtively.","A little later, she sneaked one eye open and glanced over to the side. Chen Su was standing by the edge of the ice lake, looking down at a jade slip in her hand. She did not seem to have noticed the little girl's small, secret movement.","Qin Jia let out a quiet sigh of relief, and carefully shifted her leg, which had gone numb from sitting still for so long.","\"Sit properly,\" Chen Su said, without even lifting her head.","Qin Jia's leg, which had just barely lifted off the ground, dropped right back down. She puffed out her cheeks and mumbled under her breath, \"Senior Sister wasn't even looking. How did she know I moved?\"","\"Divine sense,\" Chen Su replied.","\"When will I get to learn divine sense?\"","\"When you reach the Foundation Establishment stage, you will naturally develop your divine sense.\"","Qin Jia's face immediately fell. Her lively, outgoing nature had not settled down at all even after she joined the immortal sect. Every day, she was either pestering her master, or trailing after Chen Su, asking one question after another.","At first, Perfected Person Binghua had thought her new little apprentice was cute and full of charm. But after just a few days, she got such a headache from the endless stream of questions that she passed Qin Jia over to Chen Su. Qin Jia was absolutely delighted by the arrangement, since she had always liked Chen Su a great deal.","Quiet fell over the ice lake again. Qin Jia closed her eyes, and tried her best to follow the cultivation method to sense the spiritual energy floating between heaven and earth.","All of a sudden, a faint warm tingle spread from her chest. The warmth was so faint that she would never have noticed it if she had not been sitting perfectly still.","Qin Jia reached for her collar on instinct, and grabbed the jade pendant tucked inside. \"Sister!\" she cried out.","Qin Jia jumped right up from the ground. The cold air that had gathered all around her scattered in an instant.","Chen Su frowned. \"Qin Jia.\"","\"Senior Sister, my sister is here!\" Qin Jia completely forgot about her cultivation lesson, and ran toward Chen Su holding the jade pendant. She was running so fast that she nearly tripped over the long hem of her robe, and stumbled forward.","\"Slow down,\" Chen Su said, reaching out to steady her.","Qin Jia did not even stop to catch her breath. She held the jade pendant high up in front of Chen Su, her voice cracking with excitement. \"Senior Sister, look! It's glowing!\"","Chen Su glanced down at the pendant. \"They have arrived,\" she said.","Qin Jia froze for a split second, then jumped for joy so hard her whole body bounced. \"Father's here! Mother's here! My sister must be here too!\" She threw her arms around Chen Su's arm and shook it hard. \"Senior Sister, I want to go to the City of Neighboring Immortals right now! This very second!\"","Chen Su glanced at the darkening sky. \"It's far too late now. The teleportation array is closed for the night.\"","The big grin on Qin Jia's face vanished at once. She looked up at Chen Su, her eyes full of disappointment. \"What about tomorrow?\" She pouted, her shoulders slumping.","Chen Su looked at her dejected little face. \"Tomorrow, when the teleportation array opens, I will take you there.\"","In the next instant, Qin Jia lit up all over again. \"Senior Sister is the best in the whole world!\" She threw herself at Chen Su and wrapped her arms around her waist, grinning so wide her teeth were on full display.","Chen Su looked at the little girl clinging to her, and sighed helplessly. \"Let go of me first.\"","\"No,\" Qin Jia mumbled, burying her face against Chen Su's sleeve.","\"Go back and continue your cultivation practice.\"","\"My sister and my whole family are here now, how could I possibly calm down enough to focus on cultivation?\"","Chen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Su was just about to respond, when a lazy voice drifted down from the top of the mountain peak. \"If you can't calm down, then you don't have to cultivate.\"","Perfected Person Binghua had appeared out of thin air above the ice lake. She wore a flowing white silk dress, standing barefoot in mid-air, her features cold and strikingly beautiful. In her hand, she held a string of bright red spirit fruits.","\"My disciple of Binghua won't get left behind by others just because she skips one night of practice,\" Perfected Person Binghua said.","Chen Su bowed and greeted her, \"Master.\"","Qin Jia immediately let go of Chen Su and spun around to run toward Perfected Person Binghua. \"Master!\"","Perfected Person Binghua swept her up into a hug, then pressed a string of spirit fruits into her hand. \"You've been missing your family, haven't you? Tomorrow, your senior sister will take you home. Bring whatever you want with you. I won't have people thinking that a disciple of mine has to go home empty-handed.\"","Qin Jia nodded so hard her braids bounced. \"I'll bring Grandfather a longevity-nourishing pill, Grandmother a soft bolt of cloth, Father and Uncle the archery gear from the immortal sect, and Mother a beautiful hairpin.\"","She paused, then counted on her fingers again earnestly. \"And I have to bring something for my elder sister too.\"","Perfected Person Binghua asked casually, \"What does your sister like?\"","Qin Jia tilted her head and thought for a long time. What did her sister like? Her gaze landed on the spirit fruits in Perfected Person Binghua's hand. \"My sister loves growing things. Back at home, she was always the one who helped Mother plant all the vegetables.\"","Perfected Person Binghua chuckled. \"Growing mundane vegetables is hardly any remarkable skill.\"","But Qin Jia said very seriously, \"The vegetables my sister grows taste better than anyone else's.\"","She took a bite of the spirit fruit in her hand. After a couple of chews, her little face crumpled up. \"Sour!\"","Perfected Person Binghua did not look the least bit concerned. \"This is a jade spirit fruit. It was never meant to be a snack for you.\"","\"Then I'll take the seeds back for my sister,\" Qin Jia declared right away. \"The ones she grows will definitely be sweeter than this one.\"","Perfected Person Binghua was amused by her. \"Spirit plants are nothing like mortal vegetables. Without spiritual energy to nourish them, the seeds might not even sprout.\"","Qin Jia did not care about that at all. She carefully tucked the half-eaten fruit pit into her storage pouch, then held out her hand to Perfected Person Binghua. \"Master, do you have more?\"","\"How many do you want?\"","\"Lots and lots.\"","Perfected Person Binghua flicked her sleeve, and over a dozen jade boxes of different shapes landed in front of Qin Jia. They were just some low-grade spirit plants and spirit rice seeds she had picked up over the years and never bothered to plant. \"Take all of them.\"","Qin Jia happily stored every last jade box away. She did not care how valuable the seeds were. In her mind, anything from the immortal sect had to be wonderful.","Down below, Qin Zhen suddenly ducked her head. The jade pendant on her chest was growing warm, and its light was getting brighter and brighter.","She understood immediately. \"Grandfather.\"","Qin Huai was outside the cave sorting out his bows and arrows, and he turned around at her call. Qin Zhen had already rushed out of the cave, the most uncharacteristically hurried she had been all year.","\"Jiajia is here.\"","Every member of the Qin family froze. The wooden bowl in Liu Zhen's hand clattered to the ground. \"What did you say?\"","Qin Zhen pulled the jade pendant out from under her collar. She looked up toward the direction of Immortal's Neighbor City, her eyes shining bright. \"The pendant is glowing. Jiajia is close by.\"","Liu Zhen's eyes welled up with tears at once. \"Let's go meet her!\"","The whole family quickly gathered their things and hurried down the mountain path. The closer they got to the foot of the mountain, the brighter the jade pendant in Qin Zhen's hand glowed. Then, through the clouds, a sword shot through the air. On the flying sword stood two figures, one tall and one small. Qin Jia spotted her family standing at the foot of the mountain from far away. She froze for a second, then leaned over the edge of the flying sword and waved as hard as she could.","\"Sister!\" Her clear voice rang out from the sky. \"Sister, I'm home!\"","She had thought she would have so many things to say. She would ask if her little sister was doing well, what the immortal sect was like, and whether Jiajia had forgotten their home in Big Tree Village. But all she did was lift her arms and wrap them tight around her little sister.","Qin Jia buried her face in her elder sister's shoulder, her voice muffled. \"Sister, I missed you so much.\"","Qin Zhen's eyes turned red, and she gently rested her hand on top of her little sister's head. \"I missed you too.\""]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: The First Appearance of Spiritual Plants","paragraphs":["More than half a year had passed since the sisters were reunited.","When they had last met, Qin Jia had excitedly told her family that she had successfully drawn qi into her body and officially embarked on the path of cultivation. She was now practicing the Ice Spirit Art personally imparted by her master, Perfected Person Binghua. In addition to cultivating every day, she also had to learn to read, identify spiritual medicines, and familiarize herself with the various rules of the cultivation world.","According to Qin Jia, her master, Perfected Person Binghua, was the strongest person in the Qingyun Sect beneath the Deity Transformation realm. Knowing that her younger sister was doing well in the Qingyun Sect, the heavy stone that had long hung over Qin Zhen’s heart finally sank halfway.","Although Linxian City had the character “immortal” in its name, it was still part of the mortal world. It was called Linxian only because the city housed a teleportation array connected to the cultivation world, through which cultivators occasionally came and went.","For mortals to enter the cultivation world through the teleportation array, it was by no means enough to simply pay some silver. The spiritual energy in the cultivation world was extremely abundant, while mortal meridians were far too fragile to withstand its impact. At best, their meridians would be damaged, leaving them bedridden for the rest of their lives. At worst, all their meridians would rupture and they would die on the spot.","This was not because the Qingyun Sect deliberately barred them. Their bodies simply could not withstand it.","Still, the matter was not entirely without a solution. If mortals consumed spiritual rice, spiritual vegetables, or low-grade spiritual plants with gentle medicinal properties over a long period of time, their meridians could be slowly nourished. It might take as little as three to five years, or as long as more than a decade. As long as they consumed enough spiritual food, their meridians would gradually adapt to spiritual energy.","The reason those princes, nobles, wealthy merchants, and powerful families in the city had moved their entire households to Linxian City was likely because they were clinging to that faint glimmer of hope.","The Qin family had already accepted this reality. They lived near Linxian City, and being able to see Qin Jia once a year was far better than being separated from her forever.","That was until Qin Jia brought back more than a dozen boxes of spiritual plant seeds.","There was no spiritual energy in Linxian City. Seeds left there would almost certainly never sprout. The Qin family did not tell Qin Jia this.","Yet the instant the seeds were buried in the soil, Qin Zhen felt an overwhelming hunger. The sensation did not belong to her. It came from the seeds underground.","Ever since she was very young, Qin Zhen had been able to sense the condition of plants. She knew which vegetables lacked water, which weeds had insects in their roots, and which trees, though seemingly lush with foliage, had already begun to rot inside.","When she was little, she had once cried in fear as she told her mother that the vegetables in the fields were speaking to her. Liu Zhen had assumed she had suffered a nightmare and gently soothed her, never taking the matter to heart. As Qin Zhen gradually grew older and realized that no one else possessed such an ability, she never mentioned it to anyone again.","But the sensations transmitted by the spiritual plant seeds were much clearer than those of ordinary plants. Waves of hunger and weakness seemed to appear directly inside her mind.","Without thinking, Qin Zhen pressed her palm against the soil. A faint warmth welled up from deep within her body, traveled down her arm into her palm, and finally seeped into the earth. The seeds underground, which had been restless and uneasy, gradually quieted down.","On the morning of the third day, the first tender shoot broke through the soil. After that, more and more seeds began to sprout. Seeds that should have rotted in ordinary soil came back to life one after another under her care. This even included several seeds that had already shriveled and blackened, having nearly lost all vitality.","Half a year passed, and the once-barren land behind the house had become lush and green.","Qin Zhen crouched at the edge of the field and placed her hand on a stalk of spiritual rice. The rice leaves trembled gently, and a feeling of fullness and joy came through them.","Qin Zhen touched several of the surrounding stalks in turn.","They were ripe.","“Zhenzhen, are you looking at the things you planted again?”","Liu Zhen returned from the mountain spring carrying a bucket of water.","Qin Zhen withdrew her hand, stood up, and brushed the dirt from her clothes. “Mother, this spiritual rice is ready. It should be ready to harvest tomorrow.”","“So soon?”","Liu Zhen walked to the edge of the field and looked at the heavy ears of rice in surprise. “Can it really be eaten?”","Wang Sumei had been drying wild vegetables in the courtyard. Upon hearing them, she hurried over as well. She stared at the spiritual rice in the field for a long while, her wrinkled face breaking into a broad smile.","“That’s wonderful. This old woman has lived for so many years, yet I’ve never eaten anything that immortals eat.”","Liu Zhen laughed. “Mother, Jiajia already said that this is merely the most ordinary spiritual rice, not some elixir of immortality.”","“The most ordinary spiritual rice is still spiritual rice.” Wang Sumei beamed. “Even the wealthy lords and madams in the city may not be able to get their hands on it.”","At those words, Qin Zhen’s gaze shifted slightly.","She knew that spiritual food was expensive. But exactly how expensive it was, no one in the Qin family knew.","The plot of land was not large. Qin Ye had originally estimated that, with the entire family working together, they could finish harvesting it in no more than one morning.","He walked into the field, grabbed a handful of rice stalks, and brought the sickle down.","Clang!","A crisp sound, like metal striking metal, rang out.","Qin Ye’s wrist went numb, and the sickle instantly bounced back. If he had not reacted quickly, the blade would have nearly slashed his arm.","“What happened?”","Qin Wen hurried over.","Everyone lowered their heads to look. A clear gap had been knocked into the sickle’s edge. By contrast, the rice stalks that had been struck only bore a faint white mark. Their outer skin had not even truly been broken.","Unwilling to believe it, Qin Ye moved to another spot and swung down with all his strength. The result was the same. After several strikes, the sickle’s edge had been completely bent, yet not a single stalk of spiritual rice had fallen.","“It looks just like rice, so how is it harder than wood?” Qin Ye frowned.","Qin Huai pondered for a moment. “These are ultimately things from the cultivation world. I’m afraid ordinary iron tools can’t be used to harvest them.”","Qin Wen suddenly remembered something. “Didn’t Jiajia bring back a sword last time?”","The sword had been an ordinary longsword given by the Qingyun Sect for its disciples to practice sword techniques. Qin Wen quickly retrieved it from the house.","Most items from the cultivation world required spiritual energy to activate. Qin Ye gripped the sword hilt with both hands and brought it down forcefully toward the spiritual rice. The instant the blade touched the stalk, an invisible resistance came up through the sword. The entire weapon suddenly grew heavy. No matter how much strength Qin Ye exerted, the blade could not move down even half an inch.","Qin Wen took the longsword and tried as well, but the result was the same.","“Looks ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍like this won’t work either.” Qin Ye reluctantly lowered the sword. “Since even this spiritual rice is an immortal object, perhaps only a cultivator can harvest it.”","“Then we’ll wait until Jiajia comes back next time.” Wang Sumei looked at the heavy ears of rice in the field. Though disappointed, she had no other choice.","“Father, let me try.”","Qin Ye froze. “This sword is heavy. You won’t be able to lift it.”","“I’m not going to swing the sword.” Qin Zhen looked toward the spiritual rice in the field. “I just want to see whether I can make it help me cut the rice.”","Although Qin Ye did not understand what she meant, he still handed her the sword.","The moment the longsword fell into her hands, Qin Zhen’s arm sank sharply. As expected, she could not truly wield the weapon.","She crouched down, gripping the sword hilt with one hand while gently pressing her other hand against the base of a nearby stalk of spiritual rice. A faint warmth welled up from deep within her body and flowed through her palm into the rice’s roots and stalk.","The spiritual rice in the field began to sway gently.","Just then, a faint breath of energy traveled along the leaves of the spirit rice and returned to Qin Zhen’s body. It was not the vitality she sent into the spirit plants every day, but a wisp of spiritual energy that the plants had naturally accumulated within themselves after ripening.","That wisp of spiritual energy flowed along her arm into her other hand before finally sinking into the hilt of the sword.","Hum...","The longsword suddenly let out an almost imperceptible, clear ring. A faint blue-green light appeared along the previously dim patterns on its blade.","Qin Zhen abruptly opened her eyes.","The longsword, which had felt as heavy as a mountain moments ago, had become slightly lighter. It was not completely weightless, but she could now slowly lift it.","She had not even truly swung the sword. The few stalks of spirit rice nearest to her simply bent to one side on their own. Their cuts were smooth and even, without damaging a single grain.","The field fell silent at once.","Qin Ye and Qin Wen stared at the faintly glowing longsword in Qin Zhen’s hand, momentarily forgetting to speak.","Wang Sumei stood stunned for a long while before cautiously asking, “Zhenzhen, do you have a spiritual root too?”","Qin Zhen’s face paled slightly. She shook her head. “Master Chen tested me. I don’t have a spiritual root.”","Qin Ye looked at the longsword in her hand. “Then how were you able to make it move?”","Qin Zhen lowered her gaze to the hilt. “I don’t know. Perhaps... they were helping me.”","She looked toward the gently swaying spirit rice before her.","The moment she finished speaking, the blue-green light on the blade rapidly dimmed. The heavy force pressed down on her arm once more. Qin Zhen nearly lost her grip on the sword and hurriedly planted its tip against the ground.","She had only cut down a few stalks of spirit rice, yet a thin layer of sweat had already appeared on her forehead.","Qin Huai noticed that something was wrong with her complexion and immediately said, “Don’t push yourself.”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “They’ve already ripened. If we don’t harvest them soon, the rice heads will weigh down and break the stalks.”","She placed her hand against the leaves of the spirit rice once more. A gentle, familiar emotion again reached her from the plants in the field.","After resting for a while, Qin Zhen borrowed another wisp of spiritual energy and slowly awakened the longsword.","Her body swayed. Liu Zhen hurried forward to support her. “Zhenzhen, are you feeling unwell?”","“No.” Leaning against her mother’s arms, Qin Zhen took a gentle breath. “I’m just a little tired.”","She looked toward the field, which had now been completely harvested.","The plot of land had seemed small, but in the end, it had yielded more than twenty pounds of spirit rice. Even uncooked, it gave off an exceedingly faint, pleasant fragrance.","Wang Sumei scooped up a handful of spirit rice, beaming with delight. “We’ll cook some tonight and have a taste.”","Qin Zhen reached out to stop her. “Grandmother, don’t cook too much. There’s a very strong force within this spirit rice. We can’t eat much at once.”","She could not explain how she knew. The moment her fingers touched the rice, she could sense the gentle yet abundant energy contained within it.","To cultivators, this spiritual energy might be insignificant. But the Qin family had never come into contact with spiritual energy before. If they ate too much at once, they might not be able to withstand it.","Wang Sumei had already grown accustomed to following Qin Zhen’s instructions regarding the fields. Hearing this, she took out only a small handful.","That evening, Liu Zhen mixed the small amount of spirit rice with ordinary millet and cooked it into a thin porridge. Once it was ready, each person received only half a small bowl.","The spirit rice was soft and sticky, with a hint of delicate sweetness. After drinking half a bowl of spirit porridge, the soreness in Qin Huai’s legs eased considerably. Wang Sumei had worked hard all her life and usually slept restlessly at night, but that day she fell into a deep sleep not long after lying down and did not wake once throughout the night.","The next morning, every member of the Qin family clearly felt somewhat lighter and more energetic upon waking. The change was not particularly dramatic, but it was enough to prove that the rumors circulating in the city were true.","Spiritual food really could nourish the bodies of ordinary people.","Inside the wooden house, the Qin family sat gathered together.","Qin Ye stared at the cloth bag for a long time, hesitation showing on his face. “I’m thinking of going into the city to ask around and find out where this spirit rice actually came from.”","The moment Qin Zhen heard this, she immediately shook her head in opposition. “Father, no. We can’t expose ourselves. It’s far too dangerous.”","“Zhenzhen is right.” Qin Huai’s expression darkened as he looked at Qin Ye in disapproval.","“Understood, Father. Then I’ll continue hunting in the mountains.”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Broken Promise","paragraphs":["Qingyun Sect, Coldjade Peak.","The chill deep within the ice lake grew heavier with each passing day. Qin Jia sat cross-legged upon the Coldjade Platform at the center of the lake, a faint white mist coiling around her. Ice-attribute spiritual energy continuously gathered into her body, and she could vaguely sense that she had touched an invisible barrier.","Perfected Person Binghua stood by the lake and watched for a long while before finally speaking.","“Your cultivation can no longer be suppressed.”","Qin Jia opened her eyes.","“Master, am I about to break through?”","“Yes.”","Perfected Person Binghua raised a hand, and a streak of spiritual light entered the center of Qin Jia’s brow.","“Your cultivation has advanced too quickly, and the spiritual power within your body has yet to fully solidify. During this retreat, you must not only break through to the next realm but also reorganize the spiritual energy flowing through your meridians.”","“It may take as little as two or three years, or as long as several decades.”","Qin Jia had been beaming with joy, but the smile on her face froze at those last words.","“Several decades?”","She counted on her fingers, then suddenly sprang to her feet atop the Coldjade Platform.","“No!”","“I still have to go home this year.”","Perfected Person Binghua shot her a glance.","“An opportunity to break through may vanish in an instant. If you return to the mortal world and then come back, you may miss this chance entirely.”","Qin Jia lowered her head and looked at the Heartbond Pendant at her chest. The pale-green crescent-shaped jade pendant glimmered faintly. After hesitating for a long while, she finally asked, “Then can I send a message to my family first?”","“You may.”","Perfected Person Binghua did not stop her.","“Find ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍a disciple who will be traveling to Neighboring Immortal City soon and have him deliver a letter for you.”","With permission granted, Qin Jia immediately hurried down Coldjade Peak. She did not know many people within the sect. Senior Sister Chen Su was away on a sect mission and would not be returning anytime soon. Most of the other disciples had never been to Neighboring Immortal City. After thinking it over, Qin Jia decided that Senior Brother Xu An was the most suitable person.","Xu An was an inner disciple who often escorted supplies for the sect in exchange for contribution points, traveling back and forth between its various branches. Like Qin Jia, he had once been brought back from the mortal world, so they had quite a bit in common. However, as cultivators, both of them were busy with their own affairs, and they were not particularly close. A few days earlier, he had mentioned that he would soon be passing through Neighboring Immortal City.","When Qin Jia found him, he was outside the Teleportation Hall, counting jade slips.","“Senior Brother Xu!”","Xu An turned around. When he saw her, a smile quickly spread across his face.","“What brings you here, Junior Sister?”","Qin Jia took a communication jade slip from her storage pouch and solemnly held it out to him.","“Are you going to Neighboring Immortal City?”","“I leave tomorrow.”","“Then could you help me deliver this to my family?”","Worried that he might not be able to find them, Qin Jia carefully explained, “They live at the foot of the mountains west of Neighboring Immortal City. There are three wooden houses there, with a large patch of plants growing behind them.”","“My father’s name is Qin Ye, and my sister’s name is Qin Zhen. You should be able to find them if you ask around nearby.”","Xu An accepted the jade slip.","“What did you write inside?”","“I told them that I’m going into seclusion to break through, and that I may not be able to return for the next few years. I won’t be able to leave freely while I’m in seclusion, and I don’t know when I’ll emerge. You must tell them that I haven’t run into any danger and that they shouldn’t worry.”","After thinking for a moment, she took another jade box from her storage pouch.","“This is for my sister as well. There are some spirit seeds inside that I found recently.”","Xu An accepted both the jade slip and the jade box.","“It’s nothing, Junior Sister. Don’t worry. Once I reach Neighboring Immortal City, I’ll deliver them personally.”","Only then did Qin Jia relax.","“Thank you, Senior Brother.”","With that, she took out another jade box and handed it to Xu An.","“This is a small token of my appreciation. I’m sorry to trouble you, Senior Brother.”","Xu An took the box and smiled. “There’s really no need for this.”","The next day, Qin Jia entered the secluded cultivation chamber deep within Coldjade Peak. After the stone door closed, Perfected Person Binghua personally activated the formation outside the chamber. Until Qin Jia successfully completed her breakthrough, no one would be able to disturb her.","That same day, Xu An departed Qingyun Sect with the sect’s convoy. However, the communication jade slip was ultimately never delivered to the Qin family, and the jade box containing the spirit seeds never found its way into Qin Zhen’s hands.","Outside Neighboring Immortal City, summer in the mountains seemed especially long. When the time of year for Qin Jia’s annual homecoming arrived, the Qin family had tidied the house early. Liu Zhen made all the snacks her daughter used to enjoy, while Qin Ye and Qin Wen did not go into the mountains for several days in a row. They simply waited at the foot of the mountain, glancing up at the sky from time to time.","The Heartbond Pendant at Qin Zhen’s chest continued to glow. They waited from dawn until sunset, but the pendant never changed.","On the first day, the Qin family was not overly worried. Perhaps something had delayed her for a day or two—the affairs of an immortal sect were surely numerous. But after three days, Qin Jia still had not appeared. After ten days, the sky remained empty of the familiar streak of sword light.","Liu Zhen could no longer sit still. Qin Ye and Qin Wen took Qin Zhen into Neighboring Immortal City, where they asked around outside the teleportation array. The people guarding the array had never heard of Qin Jia, and they certainly were not going to contact Qingyun Sect on behalf of a few mortals.","Qin Ye tried asking people to approach the cultivators entering and leaving the teleportation array, but those cultivators were always in a hurry.","Some ignored them completely. Others complained that they were in the way. A few merely left them with a single remark:","“It’s perfectly normal for a disciple of an immortal sect to spend decades in seclusion or traveling.”","The Qin family could only return home in disappointment.","A month passed, and Qin Jia still had not come back. Although the light on the Heartbond Pendant had weakened, it had never gone out, and no cracks had appeared across the surface of the jade. This meant that Qin Jia was still alive.","Qin Huai could only console everyone.","“Perhaps Jiajia is in seclusion. It’s not unusual for cultivators to spend several months cultivating.”","The Qin family accepted this explanation and continued to wait.","They waited for an entire year.","When the appointed day arrived the following year, the Qin family once again went into the city and stood outside the teleportation array for seven full days. Qin Jia still did not appear.","In the third year, they paid a merchant who often did business with cultivators to inquire about Qingyun Sect.","The merchant took their silver, but returned with only one vague response:","“Everything is as usual at Qingyun Sect.”","As for where Qin Jia was, whether she was in seclusion, or when she might emerge, outsiders had no way of knowing.","It was not that the Qin family had never tried to find her.","Over the years, whenever they heard that a cultivator had entered Neighboring Immortal City, they would find a way to approach and ask about her. They had even asked others to deliver letters to Qingyun Sect, but they never received a response.","They had done nearly everything they could. The only proof that Qin Jia was still alive was the thin thread of azure light on Qin Zhen’s chest, which had never once gone out.","At the same time, the Qin family’s life was quietly changing as well.","After the first harvest of spirit rice, Qin Zhen kept most of it as seed. As she grew increasingly familiar with that mysterious power, the fields behind the wooden house gradually expanded.","At first, there had only been a few plots of land. Later, there was one mu, then two. Eventually, even the slopes below the mountain were cultivated into spirit fields. Though there was no spiritual energy in the area, the spirit rice and spirit vegetables continued to grow under Qin Zhen’s care.","Every day, the Qin family ate some of them.","One year, two years, three years...","The power within the spirit food gradually seeped into their flesh and meridians. Qin Huai’s once-graying hair slowly returned to its original black, while the hidden injuries Qin Ye and Qin Wen had sustained in their youth healed one after another. Liu Zhen and Wang Sumei’s health also became far better than before.","Although they had no spiritual roots and still could not absorb spiritual energy on their own, their bodies were no longer those of ordinary mortals. The changes in Qin Zhen were especially apparent. As the years passed, her sensitivity to spirit plants grew increasingly acute.","All these years, she had never stopped studying her ability. Little by little, she came to realize that she might truly be capable of entering that place mortals could never reach.","In the fifth year, Qin Jia still had not returned. On the night her expected return date passed, the Qin family gathered around the table, yet no one spoke for a long while. Qin Zhen’s Heartlink Pendant lay on the table. The jade pendant still glowed, but that faint light could only prove that Qin Jia was still alive.","“I’m going to the cultivation world to find her.”","Qin Ye finally broke the silence.","“I’m Jiajia’s father. I can’t keep waiting like this.”","“Father, you can’t go.”","Qin Zhen immediately shook her head.","“We don’t know what the cultivation world is like. Father, you’re too straightforward. If you run into someone with ill intentions, it would be easy for them to trick you into revealing things about our family.”","Qin Ye frowned.","“That still doesn’t mean I can let a young woman like you take such a risk.”","“I’m not going deep into the cultivation world right away.”","Qin Zhen looked toward the depths of the forest.","“I’ll only try to see whether I can cross the barrier.”","The Qin family had hunted in the nearby mountains for years and had long since discovered an invisible barrier deep within the forest. The rocks and trees beyond it were clearly visible, yet whenever an ordinary person approached, they would be stopped by an unseen force. They had always suspected that this was the boundary between the mortal realm and the cultivation world.","In the past, none of the Qin family had dared to approach it for real. But things were different now. Five years of nourishment from spirit food had gradually allowed their meridians to adapt to spiritual energy. Qin Zhen could even activate the low-grade sword Qin Jia had left behind. She might not be able to cultivate, but that did not necessarily mean she could not enter the cultivation world.","Qin Huai remained silent for a long time before finally asking, “What will you do if you’re able to cross over?”","“I won’t go far. First, I’ll investigate the area around the barrier and find somewhere inhabited. Then I’ll think of a way to ask about the Qingyun Sect. If I can’t get in, I’ll return immediately. If I can, then at least it will prove that we still have a way to find Jiajia.”","Silence once again fell over the room. They had already waited five years. If they continued to stay here, all they could do was guard the faint glimmer on the pendant—they could accomplish nothing else.","At last, Qin Huai slowly closed his eyes and let out a heavy sigh.","“Let Zhenzhen go and try, but she may only move around near the barrier. If she notices anything wrong, she must return immediately.”","On the day of her departure, the sky was still pale with dawn. Qin Zhen changed into a coarse cloth outfit that was convenient for traveling, strapped the long sword her sister had left behind to her back, and hid a short knife at her waist. Her backpack contained ten pounds of ordinary rice, several spirit vegetables, and a small amount of dried spirit-rice seeds.","The ordinary food would help conceal her identity. As for the spirit plants, they were the only thing she could rely on in the unfamiliar cultivation world.","Before she left, Liu Zhen straightened her collar.","“Zhenzhen, whether you find Jiajia or not, don’t push yourself.”","Qin Ye tried several times to speak, but in the end, he merely placed a heavy hand on his daughter’s shoulder.","Qin Zhen nodded. “I know.”","She closed her fingers around the Heartlink Pendant at her chest, which still gave off a faint glow, then turned and walked into the forest."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Vegetation Leads the Way","paragraphs":["The moment Qin Zhen stepped through the barrier, an invisible force pressed head-on against her. The air all around seemed to thicken abruptly, and icy cold breath surged into her body through her nose and mouth, making her chest feel tight and sending a fine, throbbing ache through her meridians.","She staggered back half a step and instinctively grabbed the trunk of a nearby tree. So this is the Cultivation Realm? Qin Zhen closed her eyes, waiting for a long while, but the searing pain she had braced for never came. The strange breath flooding into her made her uncomfortable, but it did not actually harm her meridians. For five full years, she had eaten nothing but spiritual rice and spiritual vegetables every day, and sure enough, her body was already strong enough to withstand the spiritual energy of the Cultivation Realm.","Yet once she had adjusted to the sensation, she quickly noticed another problem. There was no path in sight at all. Towering ancient trees blocked out the sky, and thick vines coiled around one another, nearly sealing off the way ahead entirely. The fallen leaves on the ground had piled up for no one knew how many years, and when she stepped down, they almost reached her ankles.","Qin Zhen looked back, and the barrier was still there behind her. Through that invisible shield, the mountains and forests of the mortal realm were clearly visible, so close she felt she could reach out and touch them. She carved a mark on a nearby tree, then tightened the strap of her bag and set off heading south.","Qin Jia had once mentioned that the Qingyun Sect lay to the south of the barrier. As long as she kept walking south, she would eventually find a place where people lived. The first few days of Qin Zhen's journey were extremely tough. The machete she had brought along could only cut through ordinary weeds. When it came to slightly thicker vines, the blade could not even leave more than a faint white mark on them.","As ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍for the long sword Qin Jia had left her, it was so heavy it felt like a solid lump of iron. Without spiritual energy to power it, it was no different from any ordinary iron weapon in the mortal world. Fortunately, this mountain forest had more plants than anywhere else, and unlike the vegetation of the mortal realm, every single plant here looked extraordinarily vibrant.","When Qin Zhen pressed her palm against a tree trunk, she could sense the faint emotions coming from the wood. Some were calm, some were wary, and some would even stretch out their branches and leaves of their own accord when she drew near. She could even sense through the tangled roots beneath the ground where there was water nearby, and where edible fruits grew.","By the seventh day, the dry rations she had brought were almost gone. Following the faint guidance from an old tree, Qin Zhen found a patch of low bushes bearing green berries beside a mountain stream.","She did not pluck them rashly. She rested her fingers on the leaves for a moment, sensing no danger, only then did she pick one, take a careful bite. The flesh was sweet and sour, and after she swallowed it, a faint wisp of warmth slowly spread through her abdomen.","After that, she survived on wild fruits, roots and clear spring water as she traveled. When she encountered vines she could not cut through, she would place one hand on the nearby plants, draw out the thinnest strand of spiritual energy from them, and use that to power her long sword for a short time.","The sword would only glow for a brief moment each time, but that moment was more than enough for her to slice through the vines blocking her way. However, each time she used it, she would be exhausted for a long while, so she would never draw the sword unless it was absolutely necessary.","The mountain forest was not devoid of wild beasts. On the twelfth night, Qin Zhen was jolted awake all of a sudden. Her chest felt tight, and all the plants around her sent her a strong sense of unease. Deep in the darkness, a pair of scarlet eyes could faintly be seen staring at her. Qin Zhen did not move. She slowly tightened her grip on her long sword and pressed her palm against the root of the tree behind her.","A warm current flowed from her palm into the soil. The next moment, the drooping vines nearby silently lifted up, piling layer upon layer in front of her, giving off a rich scent of plants and trees.","The wild beast in the darkness lingered for a long time, but in the end it did not come close. It was not until that dangerous aura had completely faded away that Qin Zhen realized her back was soaked through with cold sweat. The only things she could rely on were these silent plants all around her. Qin Zhen drifted off to sleep again, and when she opened her eyes, she found she was almost completely buried in grass.","\"What's going on?\"","Last night before she fell asleep, she had clearly cleared the area around her, but after just one night, the grass that had only reached her ankles had now grown as tall as her waist. The slender leaves brushed lightly against her arm, conveying a feeling of affection and joy.","Qin Zhen reached out and touched the grass blades, and the grass immediately scrambled to press toward her palm.","They seemed to love the aura coming from her body. Qin Zhen looked down at her own hand, puzzled.","Since she had entered the Cultivation Realm, her connection with the plants had grown clearer and clearer. Every time she fell asleep, that wisp of warmth inside her body seemed to seep out on its own. The plants of the mortal realm would only become a little more lively after absorbing that warmth, but the vegetation of the Cultivation Realm already contained spiritual energy. Once they received her power, their growth rate would become astonishingly fast.","\"Could this really be because of me?\"","Qin Zhen was full of questions, but she had no time to delve into them. She gently brushed the grass aside.","\"I have to keep going.\"","The grass blades clung to her clothes' hem reluctantly, and Qin Zhen patted the leaves to soothe them. The grass then slowly loosened, lying flat to both sides to make a narrow path for her.","Qin Zhen froze for a moment. This was the first time plants had responded to her thoughts so clearly. She walked along the path the grass had made for her.","That day, all the plants in the mountain forest seemed to know she was looking for an exit. Vines pulled their branches back of their own accord, and low shrubs parted to both sides. Whenever she walked in the wrong direction, the leaves nearby would send a wave of anxious emotion.","Guided by the plants, her speed increased a great deal. Three days later, the towering ancient trees that had blocked out the sky gradually thinned out, and sunlight spilled down through the gaps in the canopy. Qin Zhen quickened her steps, pushed aside the last patch of shrubs, and the view before her opened up completely."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: South Pacify City","paragraphs":["In the distance, an enormous city stood nestled among the mountains. Its walls rose dozens of zhang high, their entire surface a lustrous white, as though the city had been carved from a single block of jade. Beneath the sunlight, they gleamed with a cool, crystalline sheen.","High in the air, great immortal cranes spread their wings, each bearing robed cultivators upon its back. Nearing the city gates, they folded their wings and descended slowly. From even higher above, streaks of sword light occasionally flashed past, while other cultivators rode spirit beasts of every shape and kind along the mountain roads.","Qin Zhen stood on the hillside for a long while without moving. Only now did she truly realize that she had entered a world utterly different from the mortal realm. So this was the sort of place her younger sister had lived in all these years.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍took a deep breath and hurried toward the city.","Above the gates were three imposing characters, their strokes sharp and forceful. Qin Zhen could not read them, but from the conversations of those waiting to enter, she learned the city’s name—Southward Comfort City.","Southward Comfort City depended on the Azure Cloud Sect. Cultivators came and went here, but many ordinary people unable to cultivate also lived within the city, so mortals were not barred from entering.","Qin Zhen followed behind the crowd and passed through the gates without trouble. Her attention was immediately drawn to the sights within the city. All manner of shops lined the broad streets in orderly rows. Some sold medicinal pills, others weapons, while before many storefronts were displayed spirit plants and materials from spirit beasts that Qin Zhen had never seen before.","Qin Zhen could not read the signs, but fortunately, many shops had simple symbols carved beside their plaques. A cauldron signified a pill-refining shop, a longsword a weapon-forging workshop, and a leaf a store that sold spirit plants. Qin Jia had told her all this the last time she returned home.","The streets bustled with people. Some cultivators had palm-sized spirit birds perched upon their shoulders, while others cradled long-eared spirit beasts in their arms. Qin Zhen was curious, but she did not dare stare at anyone for too long, only stealing an occasional glance.","What she needed most now were spirit stones. Gold and silver from the mortal world could buy nothing in the cultivation world. After observing the shops along the street for some time, Qin Zhen finally stopped before an elegantly decorated establishment.","A gauzy curtain, thin as cicada wings, hung across the entrance. Through it, she could clearly see tables and chairs inside, as well as patrons eating their meals.","It seemed to be a restaurant. Qin Zhen lifted the delicate curtain and stepped inside. The moment she entered, a rich, inviting fragrance washed over her.","It had been a long time since she had eaten a proper meal. At the scent of food, her stomach gave a soft rumble. A woman dressed in a crimson-red gown came forward to greet her. She first glanced at the mud-stained hem of Qin Zhen’s clothes, then noticed the longsword on her back, yet her face showed no disdain.","“Little girl, are you here to eat?”","Qin Zhen shook her head.","“Big sister, I don’t have any spirit stones.”","The woman paused slightly. Qin Zhen continued, “I’ve just come out of the mountains and am looking for work in exchange for food and a place to stay.”","“I can chop firewood, carry water, and clean the courtyard.”","The woman looked Qin Zhen over from head to toe. Though the little girl’s clothes were worn and tattered, she was neat and clean, and she spoke clearly. She did not seem like one of the ordinary beggar children in the city. Still, Fragrant Elegance Pavilion already had enough servants and had no need for more hands.","The woman was about to refuse when a quarrel suddenly erupted from the rear courtyard.","“This batch of Green Jade vegetables was perfectly fine yesterday. How did they all wilt overnight?”","“Manager, I truly wasn’t slacking off!”","“I watered them exactly as the spirit-plant master instructed. The spirit-gathering formation is working properly too, but they just won’t recover.”","“The City Lord’s Manor is hosting a banquet tomorrow. If we can’t gather enough spirit vegetables, how is Fragrant Elegance Pavilion supposed to answer for it?”","Qin Zhen had not paid much attention at first. But when the door to the rear courtyard was pushed open, an overwhelming sensation of discomfort and suffocation suddenly flooded her mind.","Her steps halted, and she looked over instinctively.","Dozens of wooden crates stood neatly arranged in the courtyard. Each crate held several palm-sized green spirit vegetables.","Their leaves still appeared emerald-green, but their edges had begun to curl slightly. From their roots, a heavy, pained emotion continuously reached Qin Zhen.","It was not a lack of water, nor was it a shortage of spiritual energy.","They could not breathe.","Qin Zhen stared at the crates for a long while. The woman in crimson robes followed her gaze.","“Do you know Green Jade vegetables?”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “No.”","“Then what are you looking at?”","Qin Zhen hesitated before answering, “The soil beneath them is packed too tightly. Their roots are blocked. They can’t breathe.”","The courtyard immediately fell silent. Then a gray-clad attendant could not help but laugh.","“Plants can breathe?”","“Where did this little girl come from? Don’t spout nonsense here.”","Yet the woman did not immediately drive her away. This batch of Green Jade vegetables was worth no small sum. The city’s spirit-plant master had already examined them and said that the spiritual energy might be out of balance, advising them to increase the supply of spirit stones. But the spirit stones in the spirit-gathering formation had already been replaced twice, and the Green Jade vegetables had only grown more wilted.","She looked at Qin Zhen. “Do you have a solution?”","Qin Zhen walked over to one of the crates and crouched beside it. She gently inserted her fingers into the soil. Though the surface was loose and soft, the earth beneath had hardened into compacted clumps.","More strangely, there was a layer of extremely fine white rootlets mixed within it.","Those rootlets did not belong to the Green Jade vegetables. They were entwined around the vegetables’ roots, quietly siphoning away the spiritual energy in the soil.","Qin Zhen closed her eyes. A greedy, restless emotion traveled up through her fingertips.","“There’s something else in the soil,” she said. “It has tangled itself around the Green Jade vegetables’ roots.”","The gray-clad attendant frowned. “We inspect them every day. How could there be anything in the soil?”","Qin Zhen did not argue. Following the place where that emotion was strongest, she brushed aside the soil and pulled a strand of white rootlet as thin as a hair from around the Green Jade vegetable’s roots.","Once it left the soil, it began to writhe like a living creature.","The crimson-robed woman’s expression changed at once.","“Spirit-Draining Vine!”","The seeds of the spirit-siphoning vine were extremely tiny and often mixed in with spiritual soil. When they first took root, they were almost impossible to notice. But once they entwined themselves around the roots of other spirit plants, they would rapidly drain away their spiritual energy. If Qin Zhen had not found them, this batch of jade-green vegetables would likely have withered completely within two or three days.","“Turn over the spiritual soil in every wooden crate!”","The woman immediately ordered,","“Pick out every last root of the spirit-siphoning vines. Not a single one can be left behind!”","The shop hands hurriedly got to work. However, the spirit-siphoning vines’ roots were tangled too tightly with those of the jade-green vegetables. Any carelessness could tear away the vegetables’ roots as well. Qin Zhen, meanwhile, could clearly sense where the vines were located.","“Here—there’s another one on the left. Don’t use too much force underneath; you’ll damage the main root.”","As she gave instructions, she held her palm near the leaves of the jade-green vegetables. A faint warmth flowed from within her body, and the curled leaves gradually unfurled. The pain they conveyed to her also eased considerably.","About an hour later, all the spirit-siphoning vines had finally been cleared away. Su Qingqing personally inspected the plants. The jade-green vegetables that had been treated first were already standing tall again, their leaves restored to their former sheen.","The way she looked at Qin Zhen immediately changed.","“Are you a spirit plant cultivator?”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “I’ve never learned any spells for cultivating spirit plants. I’ve just always been rather good at growing things.”","Su Qingqing clearly did not entirely believe her. Even spirit plant cultivators had failed to notice the spirit-siphoning vines, yet Qin Zhen had located them so precisely. How could she merely be “rather good at growing things”?","But Qin Zhen was unwilling to say more, and Su Qingqing did not press the matter. Everyone had their own secrets.","“My name is Su Qingqing. I’m the proprietor of Fragrant Elegance Pavilion.”","She took five low-grade spirit stones from her storage pouch and handed them to Qin Zhen.","“The batch of jade-green vegetables you saved is worth far more than this. But as a mortal, carrying too many spirit stones would only make you an easy target for trouble.”","“These five spirit stones are your reward for today.”","Then she pointed to a small room in the back courtyard.","“Fragrant Elegance Pavilion has been needing someone to tend to its spirit vegetables.”","“If you are willing, you may stay here for the time being and help inspect the spirit vegetables delivered each day. I’ll provide food and lodging, and pay you another ten low-grade spirit stones every month.”","Qin Zhen did not agree immediately.","“I still need to find my younger sister. She is a disciple of the Azure Cloud Sect.”","Su Qingqing raised her brows slightly.","“The Azure Cloud Sect?”","Qin Zhen nodded. “Her name is Qin Jia. She hasn’t returned home in five years. We have received no news from her, so I entered the cultivation world to look for her.”","Su Qingqing considered this for a moment.","“The Azure Cloud Sect has countless disciples. It won’t be easy to make inquiries based on a name alone. However, South Fufeng City falls under the Azure Cloud Sect’s jurisdiction, and Fragrant Elegance Pavilion receives many Azure Cloud Sect disciples every day. If you stay here and work, it may be more convenient than searching the streets by yourself.”","Qin Zhen’s heart stirred. She had only just arrived and could not read the writing of the cultivation world. Nor did she know where the Azure Cloud Sect’s mountain gate was located. Even if she did encounter one of its disciples, they might not be willing to pay attention to an unfamiliar mortal. Staying at Fragrant Elegance Pavilion was indeed the safest and most practical option for now.","“Alright,” Qin Zhen said earnestly.","“I’ll stay, but only until I find my younger sister.”","Su Qingqing smiled.","“Of course.”","She had an attendant prepare Qin Zhen a bowl of hot food, then instructed someone to lead her to a small room in the rear courtyard to rest. Sitting at the table and gazing at the steaming meal before her, Qin Zhen finally felt the tension that had gripped her for over a month ease somewhat.","At the very least, she had entered the world of cultivation—and found a place where she could get close to disciples of the Azure Cloud Sect."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: News","paragraphs":["“Zhenzhen has been gone for so long without sending any word. It seems she must have made it through safely.”","In the fields, Qin Huai swung his hoe, hacking up a weed that had just poked its head above the soil. Even as he worked, he could not help muttering about his granddaughter, who had gone so far away.","“I only hope she’s safe in there.”","Madam Wang sat beside the field ridge, weaving the vines they had just gathered. At those words, her hands paused slightly, and she too looked toward the forested mountains to the south.","“Yes. Ye and Wen go to the area near the barrier every day to take a look. They’re hoping for any sign of movement.”","Ever since Qin Zhen had passed through the barrier, her family had been unable to learn anything about her. They only knew that Qin Zhen had successfully entered the cultivation world, but not where she was now, whether she had found Qin Jia, or whether she had encountered any danger.","Qin Huai said nothing more. He merely swung his hoe with noticeably greater force than before.","At the same time, deep within Cold Jade Peak of the Azure Cloud Sect.","Cold air filled the sealed cave abode. Qin Jia sat cross-legged atop a platform of cold jade, a thin layer of frost covering her brows, eyes, and hair. Her eyes were tightly closed as the surrounding ice-element spiritual energy continuously surged into her body.","The half-moon-shaped jade pendant hanging against her chest suddenly flickered faintly.","A weak green light flashed and vanished in an instant. Qin Jia’s lashes trembled slightly.","“Elder Sister...”","A vague murmur faded into the icy air, and soon the cave abode fell silent once more.","Nanfeng City, the rear courtyard of Fragrant Elegance Residence.","“Little Zhen, I heard you’ve found out something about your younger sister?”","Su Qingqing leaned against the doorway, smiling as she looked at Qin Zhen, who was crouched beside the spirit field. Qin Zhen was checking each of the emerald-jade vegetables in the courtyard. She lightly brushed her fingertips over the green leaves, and only after confirming that none of the plants’ roots had any problems did she rise to her feet.","“Yes, Sister Su. Yesterday, one of the guests who came to Fragrant Elegance Residence for a meal happened to be an outer disciple of Cold Jade Peak.”","At the mention of this, Qin Zhen’s expression finally relaxed somewhat.","“She said that Jiajia is in seclusion on Cold Jade Peak, attempting a breakthrough. She’s not in any danger.”","Although that outer disciple did not know Qin Jia personally, Cold Jade Peak was home only to Perfected Person Binghua’s lineage. Qin Jia was Perfected Person Binghua’s direct disciple, and she had not appeared in the sect for several years. She was indeed most likely in seclusion.","At least, she had not encountered any danger.","“That’s wonderful news.”","Su Qingqing offered her congratulations with a smile before asking, “Now that you know your younger sister is safe, are you still planning to remain in Nanfeng City and wait for her to emerge from seclusion? When cultivators enter seclusion to attempt a breakthrough, it may take as little as several months or as long as several years.”","Qin Zhen shook her head.","“I’m not going to wait any longer. Since Jiajia was safe before entering seclusion, she’ll naturally return home once she comes out. I’ve been gone for so long, and my family must be terribly worried about me. I’ll go back first and tell them that my younger sister is safe.”","Hearing this, Su Qingqing immediately looked disappointed.","“You’re leaving so soon? I was hoping to keep you at Fragrant Elegance Residence forever.”","Over the past two months, Qin Zhen had not learned a single spirit-plant cultivation technique, yet she could easily identify problems with the spirit vegetables. Which plant needed water, which had insects in its roots, and which patch of spirit soil contained too much spiritual energy—she could determine all of it with near-perfect accuracy simply by touching it.","Fragrant Elegance Residence had employed spirit-plant cultivators before, but when it came to caring for spirit plants, not one of them could compare with Qin Zhen. Su Qingqing was reluctant to see her leave, but she had no intention of stopping her.","Leaving aside the fact that Qin Zhen had a younger sister who was a direct disciple of the Azure Cloud Sect, just this ability to care for spirit plants alone meant that her future achievements might be extraordinary.","“Little Zhen, when you become successful in the future, don’t forget about your sister here.”","Qin Zhen replied earnestly, “Don’t worry, Sister Su. The next time I come to Nanfeng City, I’ll definitely visit you. Thank you for taking care of me these past two months.”","If Su Qingqing had not taken her in, Qin Zhen might not even have had a place to stay when she first entered the cultivation world.","“All right, there’s no need to be so formal between us.”","Su Qingqing waved her hand.","“Go pack your things first. Near the east gate of Nanfeng City, there’s a teleportation formation leading to Neighboring Immortal City. Taking the teleportation formation will be much faster than crossing the mountains and forests again.”","Qin Zhen’s eyes immediately lit up.","“It can take me directly back to Neighboring Immortal City?”","“Of course.”","Su Qingqing could not help laughing.","“Otherwise, do you think everyone entering or leaving the cultivation world has to spend more than a month traveling through the mountains and forests like you did?”","Qin Zhen was delighted. She immediately turned and headed toward the small room where she lived.","“You little girl, why are you in such a hurry?”","Su Qingqing called out from behind her. Qin Zhen halted and turned back in confusion, only to see Su Qingqing take out a small cloth pouch and casually toss it over.","Qin Zhen hurriedly caught it. The pouch was surprisingly heavy. When she opened it, she found fifty lower-grade spirit stones neatly arranged inside.","“Sister Su, this is...”","“The teleportation formation costs fifty lower-grade spirit stones per use.”","Leaning against the doorframe, Su Qingqing spoke in a casual tone.","“Take them. They’re exactly enough to get you back to Neighboring Immortal City.”","Qin Zhen quickly held the pouch out again.","“No, Sister Su. This is too much.”","“I’ve been eating and staying at Fragrant Elegance Residence for the past two months without doing anything to repay you. Why don’t I stay for a few more months and return home after I’ve earned enough?”","“If you stay for several more months, your family will probably be frantic with worry.”","Su Qingqing did not take the pouch.","“These fifty spirit stones aren’t a gift. Consider them an investment I’m making in advance.”","She spoke half-jokingly. “If you really become some great spirit-plant master in the future, you mustn’t forget that you owe me this favor.”","Qin Zhen held the pouch in both hands and remained silent for a long while. She did not want to incur such a significant debt of gratitude for no reason.","But when she thought of her grandparents, parents, and uncle waiting at home for news of her, she found herself unable to refuse.","“Thank you, Sister Su.”","Qin Zhen carefully put away the spirit stones.","“I’ll remember what you’ve done for me today.”","“If I ever have the chance, I’ll repay you.”","“All right, that’s enough.”","Su Qingqing waved dismissively.","“Hurry up and pack. The teleportation formation can only be activated a limited number of times each day. If you miss the last trip today, you’ll have to wait until tomorrow.”","With that, she turned and walked into Fragrant Elegance Residence. Qin Zhen stood where she was, watching her retreating figure, and silently engraved this debt of gratitude in her heart.","Before long, she had packed her belongings. Compared to when she had first arrived in Nanfeng City, there was not much more in her bundle. The ordinary food her family had prepared for her before she left had already been eaten, leaving only a small bag of spirit-rice seeds and a few personal items.","Aside from those, she had only the small amount of spirit stones she had saved over the past two months.","Qin Zhen slung the bundle over her back, tied the long sword her younger sister had left behind across her back, and hurried toward the eastern part of the city. By the time she arrived at the teleportation formations, the sky had already begun to darken.","Several teleportation formations of various sizes were spread across the spacious plaza, with lines of people waiting before each one. Qin Zhen stood to the side and observed for a while. By following the symbols beside the formations and listening to the conversations of passing travelers, she finally located the line for Neighboring Immortal City.","She hurried over. The line was not particularly long, and it was soon her turn. The cultivator in charge of guarding the teleportation array sat behind a wooden desk. Without even looking up, he simply held out a hand.","“Fifty low-grade spirit stones.”","Qin Zhen handed over the spirit stones Su Qingqing had given her. The cultivator swept them with his divine sense, confirmed that the amount was correct, and raised a hand to point ahead.","“Go in. This is the last trip today. If you’re any later, you’ll have to wait until tomorrow.”","At that, Qin Zhen hurried into the teleportation array.","The array was circular, its floor carved with intricate silver patterns. Several dozen people were already standing inside. Qin Zhen could only carefully make her way to the outermost edge, doing her best not to bump into anyone.","Before long, the cultivator guarding the array embedded a spirit stone into the array’s core.","The patterns on the ground lit up one after another. Blinding white light shot into the sky, instantly enveloping everyone within.","In the next moment, every figure in the teleportation array vanished. Qin Zhen’s vision went white, followed immediately by a violent wave of dizziness. It felt as though countless forces were squeezing her from all directions at once. Her chest tightened, and her internal organs seemed to be churning together. Her legs went weak, and she nearly lost her balance.","Qin Zhen bit her lip hard, struggling to remain conscious.","She didn’t dare close her eyes. She knew the teleportation would take only a moment, yet time seemed to stretch endlessly. She had no idea how long passed before that suffocating pressure finally began to fade.","The solid ground returned beneath her feet. Qin Zhen steadied herself against a nearby stone pillar and cautiously opened her eyes.","The people around her looked just as miserable. Some had only just managed to regain their footing when they began complaining.","“The teleportation array in Nanfu City is getting worse and worse.”","“No kidding.”","Another person rubbed his chest, his face pale.","“I ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍wonder how long it’s been since they last repaired it. These past few years, every time I travel to the Mortal Realm, I have to suffer through this.”","“Do you really think the people in charge of the city care whether we live or die?”","“As long as the array can still operate and collect spirit stones, they can’t be bothered to spend money repairing it.”","“Next time, I’m not traveling from Nanfu City.”","“I’d rather take the long way around and use the teleportation array in Yuxian City.”","Someone beside them shook his head when he heard that.","“The teleportation array in Yuxian City is stable enough, but each trip costs two hundred low-grade spirit stones.”","“Nanfu City is the closest to the Mortal Realm and charges only fifty. Other than here and Yuxian City, there isn’t a third teleportation array to the Mortal Realm anywhere nearby.”","“Even if it costs more, it’s still better than suffering.”","“That’s easy for you to say. You have the spirit stones.”","The group continued grumbling as they walked out of the teleportation array.","Qin Zhen stood among the crowd, her face still somewhat pale, but her heart was already overflowing with joy.","Linxian City.","She was finally home.","Qin Zhen tightened her grip on the Heartbound Pendant at her chest. Ignoring her physical discomfort, she hurried out of the teleportation array. She couldn’t wait to return home.","To tell everyone...","Jiajia hadn’t met with any misfortune. She was merely in secluded cultivation."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Qin Zhen Returns Home","paragraphs":["“Mother!”","“Father! Grandfather, Grandmother, Uncle!”","Familiar voices came from outside the courtyard. They drew closer and closer, accompanied by a burst of light, hurried footsteps. Liu Zhen, who was clearing away the dishes in the kitchen, trembled from head to toe. The coarse pottery bowl in her hand nearly slipped to the floor, and she looked up in disbelief.","“Zhenzhen?”","Qin Ye and the others in the courtyard stopped what they were doing at the same time. In the next moment, a small figure dashed through the courtyard gate and raced toward them.","“I’m home!”","“It’s Zhen’er!”","Liu Zhen’s eyes reddened at once. She did not even have time to leave the kitchen before Qin Zhen had already thrown herself into her arms.","“Zhen’er, my Zhen’er...”","Liu Zhen held her long-lost daughter tightly, her palm stroking Qin Zhen’s back again and again as tears streamed down her face. Qin Zhen buried her face against her mother’s chest, her voice muffled.","“Mother, I’m sorry I made you worry.”","“Your daughter is home.”","“As long as you’re home.”","Liu Zhen hugged her without the slightest intention of letting go, repeating over and over:","“As long as you came back safely. As long as you came back safely...”","Qin Ye stood to one side. His lips moved several times, but he could not bring himself to speak. Only after confirming that his daughter was uninjured did he finally let out a long breath and raise his hand to vigorously ruffle Qin Zhen’s hair.","“Why didn’t you call out in advance when you got back? You nearly made your mother drop the bowls.”","Though he said this, his eyes were red as well. Qin Wen was already circling Qin Zhen excitedly.","“My niece is finally back!”","“If you’d stayed away any longer, your father would have taken me to force our way through the barrier.”","“What nonsense are you spouting?”","Qin Ye glared at his younger brother, though he did not deny it. Looking at the family gathered around her, the tension that had kept Qin Zhen on edge finally melted away completely.","“Let the child come inside first,” Qin Huai said. “You can talk after we’ve eaten.”","Wang Sumei hurriedly wiped the corners of her eyes.","“That’s right. Zhenzhen has been traveling for so long—she must be starving. Grandmother will fry a couple more dishes for you.”","The whole family escorted Qin Zhen inside. At the dinner table, Liu Zhen kept piling food into her daughter’s bowl, as though she wished she could heap everything on the table in front of her.","While eating, Qin Zhen slowly recounted everything that had happened over the past few months.","She told them about wandering through the mountains and forests for more than a month, about how the plants and trees had shown her the way, and about meeting Su Qingqing, the proprietor of Fragrant Elegance Residence, after entering Nanfu City. Su Qingqing had taken her in, and Qin Zhen had helped care for the spirit vegetables there.","The members of the Qin family grew tense at times and marveled at others. When they heard that Qin Zhen had encountered wild beasts in the mountains, Liu Zhen’s face turned deathly pale. She gripped her daughter’s hand and refused to let go for a long while.","It was not until Qin Zhen brought up Qin Jia that the atmosphere in the room finally settled.","“I met an outer disciple of Cold Jade Peak at Fragrant Elegance Residence.”","Qin Zhen set down her chopsticks.","“She said Jiajia is currently in closed-door cultivation, attempting a breakthrough. She hasn’t come back these past few years not because she encountered any danger, but because she cannot leave during her seclusion.”","Liu Zhen quickly asked, “Is Jiajia safe?”","“She’s safe.”","Qin Zhen nodded.","“The Heartbound Jade hasn’t gone out, and nothing major has happened at Cold Jade Peak. Once she succeeds in her breakthrough, she’ll naturally come out of seclusion.”","The tension that had weighed on Qin Ye’s shoulders for five years finally eased.","“As long as she’s safe.”","Wang Sumei clasped her hands together and murmured softly, “Thank Heaven. Thank Heaven.”","Qin Huai said nothing. He merely lifted his bowl and took a sip of soup. The wrinkles on his face relaxed, and the relief in his eyes was unmistakable. After five years of waiting in anguish, the enormous stone suspended over the Qin family’s hearts had finally fallen.","The atmosphere at the dinner table gradually grew livelier. Qin Wen pestered Qin Zhen with questions about what the cultivation world was like, while Wang Sumei kept asking about food, clothing, housing, and transportation in Nanfu City. Even Qin Ye, who was usually quiet, could not help asking several questions about whether flying on a sword was truly possible.","After everyone had eaten their fill, Qin Zhen slowly set down her bowl and chopsticks. She looked at the family members around the table, and her expression gradually turned solemn.","“Grandfather, Grandmother, there’s one more thing I’d like to discuss with everyone.”","Noticing the change in her tone, everyone fell silent. Qin Zhen took a deep breath.","“I think our whole family could move into the cultivation world.”","The moment she finished speaking, the room fell utterly silent. Qin Wen still had half a mouthful of rice in his mouth. After staring blankly for a moment, he finally managed to swallow it.","“Move into the cultivation world?”","Wang Sumei looked uneasy as well.","“Zhenzhen, didn’t Master Chen say that mortals can’t withstand the spiritual energy in the cultivation world? If they enter recklessly, they’ll die.”","“That was true before.”","Qin Zhen explained, “But our family has been eating spirit rice and spirit vegetables for several years now. Grandfather and Grandmother are much healthier than they used to be, and the old injuries Father and Uncle suffered when they were young have disappeared as well. Our meridians have already been nourished by spirit food, so we may not be as unable to withstand spiritual energy as ordinary mortals.”","“At the very least, when I passed through the barrier, I felt uncomfortable at first, but I wasn’t actually injured.”","Qin Huai’s eyes flickered.","“You want us to try passing through the barrier as well?”","“Mm.”","Qin Zhen nodded seriously.","“The cities in the cultivation world aren’t actually that different from those in the mortal world. They have shops, inns, restaurants, and ordinary people too. The only difference is that there are cultivators, along with many methods unique to immortals. We don’t necessarily have to live inside the city. There are mountains and forests outside Nanfu City, as well as land that can be cultivated.”","“We can find a place outside the city and settle down just as we have here. Father and Uncle can hunt, Grandfather can make bows and arrows, and Mother and Grandmother can grow vegetables and cook.”","When she spoke of farming, Qin Zhen’s tone became more confident.","“I worked at Fragrant Elegance Residence for two months. They hired spirit plant masters to care for the spirit vegetables, but what they grew may not have been as good as what our family can grow. Our spirit rice and spirit vegetables not only grow faster, their spiritual energy is also gentler and purer.”","“In the cultivation world, spirit rice and spirit vegetables are very expensive. Cultivators use them to prepare spirit food and refine fasting pills. Even ordinary mortals living in the cities can rarely afford to eat spirit rice every day. Most of them still eat ordinary grains, though because those grains are nourished by the spiritual energy there, they’re better than the food in the mortal world.”","Wang Sumei stared at her in a daze.","“So you’re saying that the things we grow can really be sold for money there? Spirit stones?”","“They can.”","Qin Zhen nodded.","“As long as we can grow spirit rice, we won’t have to worry about making a living. Besides, the spiritual energy in the cultivation world is abundant, so even ordinary mortals live longer there. Sister Su said that as long as they’re healthy, it isn’t unusual for someone who cannot cultivate to live to a hundred.”","She looked down at the Heartbound Jade hanging against her chest.","“Most importantly, once we move into the cultivation world, we’ll be closer to Jiajia. When she comes out of seclusion, we won’t have to wait bitterly for her to return just once a year.”","Silence fell over the room once more. The Qin family had only arrived in Neighboring Immortal City a few years ago, and they had finally managed to settle down. Now they would have to move again—to a completely unfamiliar place.","This was by no means a decision that could be made lightly. Qin Zhen was usually a woman of few words, but now that she had said so much in one breath, she was so nervous that her fingers unconsciously clenched the hem of her clothes.","Qin Huai pondered for a long while, his palm slowly rubbing the wooden cane beside him. Ever since he had begun eating spiritual food every day, his health had steadily improved. The cane that had once never left his side had long since become unnecessary.","“Are you certain we can pass through the barrier?” Qin Huai asked solemnly.","“I can’t be completely certain.”","Qin Zhen did not try to conceal the truth.","“But I think it’s worth a try. The first time, Father and Uncle can go through. If they feel unwell, they can immediately come back. Once we’re sure there’s no danger, Grandfather, Grandmother, and Mother can cross over as well.”","Qin Huai slowly nodded. Although this plan still carried some risk, it was far safer than having the entire family charge in recklessly.","After hesitating for a moment, Qin Zhen continued, “Also, I think Father, Mother, and Uncle might be able to try cultivating.”","“What?”","Qin Wen abruptly raised his head. His face was filled with disbelief, but his eyes suddenly lit up.","“Big Niece, I’m already this old. Can your Uncle still cultivate immortality?”","Liu Zhen was stunned as well.","“Zhenzhen, you mean your mother might be able to, too?”","“I can’t be sure.”","Qin Zhen shook her head.","“Back then, Master Chen only tested Jiajia and me for spiritual roots. She never tested Father, Mother, or Uncle.”","“She said that children under ten were more likely to draw qi into their bodies. But she only said that younger children had an easier time. She never said adults absolutely couldn’t cultivate.”","“All these years, our entire family has eaten spiritual rice and spiritual vegetables every day. The hidden injuries Father and Uncle suffered when they were young have already healed, and Mother’s health is also much stronger than before.”","“Spiritual food doesn’t merely improve the body. It also nourishes the meridians over time.”","She thought carefully for a moment before continuing.","“Father, Mother, and Uncle are all still fairly young. If you had spiritual roots all along but simply never had the chance to have them tested as children, then it may not be impossible for you to try drawing qi into your bodies now.”","Qin Ye’s breathing immediately quickened.","“Zhenzhen, is that really true?”","“I only think it’s possible.”","Qin Zhen did not make any firm promises.","“Whether you can cultivate or not, we’ll first have to find a way to test for spiritual roots. Even if you do have them, your cultivation speed will probably be inferior to Jiajia’s because of your age. But as long as you can draw qi into your body, you’ll have truly set foot on the path of immortality.”","Liu Zhen lowered her head and stared at her hands, her expression dazed. She had never imagined that one day the words “cultivate immortality” might apply to her as well.","In the past, all she had hoped for was that her two daughters would remain safe and healthy. Qin Jia possessed an exceptional ice spiritual root, and Liu Zhen had been delighted for her. When Qin Zhen was found to have no spiritual roots, Liu Zhen could not help but feel heartbroken for her. As for whether she herself could cultivate, she had never once considered it.","Qin Wen was already grinning from ear to ear.","“If I really do have spiritual roots, will I be able to fly on a sword someday?”","Qin ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Huai glared at him.","“They haven’t even tested your spiritual roots yet, and you’re already thinking about flying.”","Qin Wen scratched his head.","“There’s no harm in imagining it.”","The atmosphere in the room relaxed slightly, but Qin Ye soon noticed something else.","“Zhenzhen, you said that your mother, your uncle, and I might have spiritual roots. What about you?”","Everyone’s eyes immediately turned back to Qin Zhen. She was silent for a moment.","“I may be different from you. I don’t have spiritual roots, so I can’t absorb the spiritual energy of Heaven and Earth directly like Jiajia can. But whenever I tend to spiritual plants, a warm current appears inside my body. It helps the spiritual plants grow, and it can also use the spiritual energy within them to drive a sword.”","“After entering the cultivation world, that power has become increasingly distinct, and my connection with plants and trees has grown much clearer than before.”","She lowered her head and looked at her palm.","“So I suspect that I may already be cultivating, only I’m walking a different path from ordinary cultivators. I have no cultivation method, and I don’t know how to proceed.”","Qin Ye shot to his feet.","“You can really cultivate?”","His voice was so loud that the bowls and chopsticks on the table trembled slightly. Qin Zhen could not help turning her head away.","“Father, keep your voice down.”","“Right, right.”","Qin Ye hurriedly lowered his voice, but there was no hiding the excitement on his face. Liu Zhen stared blankly at her daughter, her eyes gradually reddening. When she had heard that she herself might possess spiritual roots, she had been surprised, but she had not immediately thought about entering the cultivation world. Now, upon learning that Qin Zhen might already have embarked on a special path of cultivation, the last of her hesitation vanished.","“We’re going.”","Liu Zhen reached out and pulled her daughter into her arms.","“We’re going to the cultivation world. Even if there’s only the slightest possibility, we can’t hold you back.”","Qin Zhen was slightly taken aback.","“Mother, you might be able to cultivate, too.”","“Whether your mother can cultivate isn’t important.”","Liu Zhen gently stroked her hair.","“If I can cultivate, that will naturally be a blessing. If I can’t, I won’t feel regret. But you have clearly found your own path. As your parents, we can’t let fear of change force you to spend the rest of your life fumbling around here.”","Qin Ye nodded firmly.","“When your sister gained her immortal opportunity, our entire family moved to Neighboring Immortal City. Now that you may also be embarking on the path of immortality, of course we’ll support you in the same way.”","“As for whether your mother, your uncle, and I can cultivate, we’ll find a place to test our spiritual roots after entering the cultivation world.”","Qin Huai remained silent for a moment before finally making his decision.","“Then we’ll go. We moved once for Jiajia. Now we’ll move again for Zhenzhen—what of it? Besides, if Ye’er, Zhen’er, and Wen’er truly possess spiritual roots, it will be an immense opportunity for the Qin family.”","Qin Wen excitedly jumped to his feet.","“I’ll go pack our things right now!”","“Stay where you are.”","Qin Huai immediately stopped him.","“Entering the cultivation world isn’t the same as going to the market. How can you leave the moment you say you will?”","“Tomorrow, Ye’er, Zhen’er, and Wen’er will each try passing through the barrier. If all three of them can cross safely, then we’ll pack up our belongings and move there as a family.”","Liu Zhen nodded.","“Good.”","“We’ll try together as a family, and we’ll leave together as a family.”"]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Moving Again","paragraphs":["\"Zhenzhen, are you awake? Mother has cooked congee for you, and also made the plum cake you love the most. Get up quickly and come eat.\"","The moment day broke, Liu Zhen's voice drifted in from outside the house.","\"Coming, Mother.\"","Qin Zhen called back, quickly dressed herself, pushed the door open and stepped out.","After a whole night to settle their thoughts, the news they brought back the day before still had not calmed the Qin family down. Entering the cultivation world and trying to practice cultivation—every single part of that felt like an unimaginable dream to them.","The whole family sat around the small table, their faces showing both anticipation and unease. No one had taken the initiative to speak, yet all their eyes turned to Qin Zhen at the same time. Holding her congee bowl, Qin Zhen felt so fidgety that she could barely sit still. She lowered her head and took a sip of the congee, and when she looked up again, everyone was still staring at her.","She simply lifted her bowl, drained the rest of the congee in one breath, then picked up a whole piece of plum cake and stuffed it into her mouth. With her cheeks puffed out like a little squirrel, she said, \"I'm done eating. Let's set off now.\"","Liu Zhen was so amused by her look that she burst into a giggle. \"What's the rush? Eat slowly, don't choke yourself.\"","Qin Zhen swallowed the plum cake with difficulty, then stood up immediately. \"I'm really finished. Let's go, let's go try it right now.\"","The tense mood that had hung over the Qin family was eased a little by her antics. Qin Huai put down his bowl and stood up slowly. \"Since everyone is ready, let's go.\"","Before long, the whole family stood in perfect order outside the formation deep in the mountains. The scene before them looked no different from an ordinary forest—ancient trees, tangled vines, and wild grass, all clearly in view. But as soon as they reached out, they could touch an invisible barrier.","None of the Qin family stepped forward right away. When they had talked about moving the day before back in the house, everyone had been excited. But now that they were actually standing here, thinking that the other side of the barrier was the legendary cultivation world, it was only natural that they felt nervous.","Qin Wen swallowed hard. \"Big niece, this is the spot you walked through before?\"","\"Yes, it is.\" Qin Zhen nodded. The moment her voice fell, she took a step forward without the slightest hesitation, and walked straight through the formation.","The rest of the Qin family were startled by her sudden move. Liu Zhen instinctively reached out her hand. \"Zhenzhen!\" But after a second, they realized that Qin Zhen had already gone through the barrier alone, and had even lived in the cultivation world for several months.","The moment she passed through the formation, rich spiritual energy surged toward Qin Zhen again. But this time, she did not feel chest tightness or swollen meridians. The cool, thick spiritual energy wrapped around her from all directions, seeping into her body with every breath. Every pore on her body seemed to open at once, and a hard-to-describe sense of comfort spread through every limb and bone.","Compared to the city of Nanfu, the plants in this forest were far more lush. The scents of countless different plants tangled together, like a warm, vast current that gently held her up. The branches and leaves nearby moved without any wind, and the low grass all bent their blades in her direction, sending out feelings of closeness and joy.","Qin Zhen could not help closing her eyes. Every part of her body seemed to be cheering. She loved this place—or rather, the plant-related power inside her loved this place. On the other side of the formation, the Qin family could no longer see Qin Zhen's figure. Liu Zhen's heart tightened. Even though she knew her daughter was safe, seeing her vanish right in front of her eyes still made her feel a little flustered.","She gritted her teeth and walked forward first. \"I'll go try it.\"","\"Zhen!\"","Wang Sumei had no time to stop her before Liu Zhen had already passed through the formation. A wave of thick spiritual energy hit her face, and Liu Zhen staggered, as if a heavy stone had been pressed onto her chest all of a sudden, making it hard to breathe. She quickly grabbed hold of a nearby tree trunk to steady herself.","\"Mother!\" Qin Zhen hurried over to support her. \"How do you feel?\"","Liu Zhen closed her eyes to steady herself for a moment. That oppressive feeling did not get any worse. After the spiritual energy flowed into her body, even though it made her meridians throb faintly, it did not do any real harm. After a while, she opened her eyes slowly. \"It's a little uncomfortable, but I can bear it.\"","Once he was sure his wife was in no danger, Qin Ye immediately stepped through the formation next, followed by Qin Wen. The moment the two of them came in, their faces also turned pale and they breathed heavily, but after standing still for a moment to adjust, they both gradually felt better.","Qin Wen moved his arms around, surprised. \"When I first came in, it felt like someone had put a stone on my chest, but now I feel much better.\" Qin Ye nodded in agreement. \"My body feels a little swollen, but there's no pain at all.\"","Qin Zhen watched the three of their expressions carefully. The reactions of her mother, father, and uncle were very similar to what she had experienced the first time she entered the cultivation world—uncomfortable, but well within the range they could tolerate.","This proved that all the years of eating spiritual rice and spiritual vegetables had truly worked. On the other side of the formation, Qin Huai and Wang Sumei were still waiting. Qin Ye walked back through the barrier again to tell the two elders what had happened inside.","After listening, Qin Huai thought for a moment. \"Since the three of you can all bear it, that means Zhenzhen's guess was right. All the spiritual food we have eaten over the years has truly changed our bodies and meridians.\"","\"Father, you and Mother shouldn't try to go in today,\" Qin Ye said. \"You two are older. Tomorrow, when we officially move in, Wen and I will stay right by your sides and go in with you slowly.\"","Qin Huai did not try to be brave, and nodded in agreement. \"I'm an old man, of course I won't risk my own health. Now that we've confirmed we can get in, we might as well go back and pack our things today, and set off properly early tomorrow morning.\"","Wang Sumei was still a little worried. She looked at Qin Zhen and asked, \"Zhen'er, the cultivation world is so big. Once we're in, where are we going to settle down? We can't just wander around the forests aimlessly with the whole family.\"","\"Grandmother, don't worry, I've already thought it through,\" Qin Zhen replied. \"The first time I walked through the formation, I walked for a very long time in the forest. On the way, I found a valley. The plants there once led me to a water source. The land there is flat, sheltered from the wind and facing the sun, and there's a stream right next to it. I didn't find any traces of large wild beasts nearby. After we clear the land, we should be able to grow spiritual rice and spiritual vegetables there. I even left marks on the trees, so we should be able to find it.\"","Wang Sumei felt a little more at ease after hearing that. \"How far is it from the cities?\"","\"It takes about a month to walk from that valley to Nanfu. It's a bit far from the city, but we don't have enough spirit stones to buy a house in the city right now. We'll live in the mountains first, farm just like we do now, and after we save up enough spirit stones, we can think about moving closer to a city later.\"","Qin Huai nodded approvingly. \"That's the best plan. Our Qin family has always lived off the mountains. We're new to the cultivation world and don't know anyone here. Living in the city would make us spend spirit stones for everything all the time. We'll settle down in the mountains first, harvest our first crop of spiritual rice, and then slowly find out more about everything else.\"","With their new destination confirmed, the Qin family no longer hesitated. That very day after returning to their log cabin, the whole family immediately set to packing their belongings. Qin Ye and Qin Wen sorted through bows, machetes, axes, and farm tools one by one, while Liu Zhen and Wang Sumei tidied up their clothes, bedding, cookware, and the remaining grain.","Qin Huai sat in the courtyard, carefully dividing the spirit rice seeds he had saved over the years into separate containers, fearing they might get damp and spoiled along the way. There were so many things they could bring with them, but when the time actually came to move, they realized some possessions simply could not be taken along. The log cabin they had built with their own hands, the fields they had cleared and cultivated, the tables and chairs they had used for years, and the fruit trees they had planted in the courtyard—all of these had to be left behind.","Wang Sumei stood in the courtyard gazing at the scene for a long time, a hint of reluctance in her eyes. They had trekked for a whole year from Big Tree Village to arrive near Immortal Neighbor City, then lived in this mountain forest for several years, transforming the wasteland into what it was now with their own labor.","Now they had to leave all of it behind. Qin Huai walked over to her side. \"Reluctant to go?\"","\"More than a little,\" Wang Sumei sighed. \"But as long as the whole family is together, it doesn't matter where we move to.\"","Qin Huai looked toward his busy sons, daughter-in-law, and grandchildren, nodding slowly. \"That's right. Wherever our family is, that's home.\"","The next day, before dawn even broke, the entire Qin family was already up. Several simple wooden carts were parked outside the courtyard gate, loaded with clothes, grain, farm tools, and spirit seeds—almost all the family's belongings they could take away.","Qin Ye and Qin Wen walked at the very front, pulling the carts, while Qin Huai and Wang Sumei sat in one of the carts. Liu Zhen followed beside it carrying a bundle on her back, and Qin Zhen stood at the courtyard gate, taking one last look at the log cabin that had been their home for years.","Morning mist draped the mountain forest. The spirit fields behind the house had already been harvested, leaving only neat rows of ridges. This place had once been where the Qin family waited for Qin Jia's return, and where Qin Zhen had grown her first spirit plant, discovering for the first time that she was different from others.","Now they were setting off once more. Their last move was for Qin Jia's immortal destiny, but this one was for the entire Qin family's future.","\"Zhenzhen, it's time to go.\"","Liu Zhen's call came from up ahead.","\"Coming.\"","Qin Zhen pulled her gaze away and quickly caught up with her family. The carts piled high with their belongings rumbled slowly into the forest. By the time they reached the barrier, the sky had already fully brightened. The several wooden carts came to a stop among the trees, carrying every last possession the Qin family had accumulated over the years.","Qin Ye steadied his cart, then turned back to his parents. \"Father, Mother, don't rush. Wen and I will take some of the things across first, then come back for you two.\"","Qin Huai waved his hand. \"We already tested it yesterday. There's no danger on the other side of the barrier—it's just a single step across. There's no need to be so overly cautious.\"","He spoke casually, but his hand gripping his wooden cane tightened unconsciously. Standing beside him, Wang Sumei stared at the invisible barrier, her face also showing clear nervousness. Yesterday, when Qin Ye and the other two had walked through the barrier, their figures had vanished from sight in an instant. Even though she knew they were right on the other side, the feeling had still been deeply unsettling.","Qin Zhen walked over to her grandfather and grandmother. \"Grandfather, Grandmother, I'll go across with you two. When you first step in, your chest might feel a little tight, and your meridians will swell. Don't rush to walk, just breathe slowly. Once your body adjusts, you'll feel much better.\"","Qin Huai nodded. \"Grandfather remembers.\" But Wang Sumei could not help asking, \"What if I can't bear the feeling?\"","\"Then we'll come right back out,\" Qin Zhen said earnestly. \"The barrier is right behind us. As long as you don't go deep further in, you can turn back any time.\"","Hearing those words, Wang Sumei felt a little more at ease. Qin Ye and Qin Wen had already stepped through the barrier first, moving some of the belongings off the carts to the other side. Liu Zhen waited on the far side of the barrier, looking toward her parents with worry. Even though the people on either side could not see each other, she did not leave her spot for a single moment.","\"Let's go,\" Qin Huai took a deep breath and stepped forward first. The moment he crossed the barrier, rich spiritual energy surged toward him. His body suddenly felt heavy, as if the air around him had turned into invisible water, pressing down on his chest with a thick weight. Icy cool breath flowed into his body as he breathed, and his previously calm meridians began to ache and swell.","His steps staggered.","\"Father!\" Qin Ye hurried forward to support him, and Qin Zhen also immediately grabbed her grandfather's arm. \"Grandfather, don't try to circulate your qi, and don't hold your breath. Breathe slowly just like you normally do.\"","Qin Huai closed his eyes, adjusting his breathing as she instructed. The initial oppressive feeling remained strong, as if a huge boulder was sitting on his chest, and even the spaces between his bones throbbed faintly. But after a few breaths, the pain did not get any worse.","The spiritual energy pouring into his body flowed slowly along his meridians, before finally sinking into his flesh and blood. Over the years, the spirit rice and spirit vegetables they had eaten had long nourished his body without him noticing. His meridians, though far less tough than a cultivator's, were already capable of withstanding the scouring of spiritual energy.","Qin Huai opened his eyes slowly. His face was a little pale, but his gaze was clear.","\"Father, how do you feel?\" Qin Ye asked anxiously.","Qin Huai tried moving his arm. \"My chest is a little tight, and my bones are a bit swollen, but I can bear it.\"","After saying that, he looked up at his surroundings. The forest on the other side of the barrier was nothing like the mortal world. Towering trees blocked out the sky, and even the grass and leaves grew exceptionally lush, brimming with vibrant life. Even with every breath he took, he could feel that cool, refreshing quality in the air.","\"So this is the Cultivation World,\" Qin Huai murmured in awe.","Confirming that his father was unharmed, Qin Ye finally relaxed a little. On the other side of the barrier, Wang Sumei was still waiting. Qin Zhen stepped back through to join her. \"Grandmother, Grandfather made it across safely.\"","Wang Sumei asked quickly, \"Is he feeling unwell at all?\"","\"He ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍felt a little tight in the chest at first, but he's already recovered,\" Qin Zhen took her grandmother's hand again. \"Grandmother, don't be afraid. I'll stay right by your side.\"","Wang Sumei looked at her granddaughter and nodded slowly. \"Fine, Grandmother isn't scared.\" Even so, the moment she stepped across the barrier, she closed her eyes instinctively. The instant the spiritual energy washed over her, Wang Sumei's face drained of all color. Her body was less robust than Qin Huai's, so the oppression hit her even harder. It felt as if a tight hand had suddenly wrapped around her chest, and her legs went weak, nearly making her fall to her knees.","\"Mother!\" Liu Zhen had been waiting on the other side, and caught her shoulders to support her at once. Qin Zhen also held her grandmother's hand firmly. \"Grandmother, breathe slowly, don't be afraid—we're all here with you.\"","Wang Sumei tried to reply, but could not speak at once. The voices around her sounded as if they were separated by a layer of water, and her body trembled uncontrollably. Qin Zhen placed one hand on the tree trunk beside her, and pressed the other against her grandmother's hand. A faint, warm current flowed from where their hands touched into Wang Sumei's body, and the grass and leaves nearby swayed gently.","Strands of gentle, herb-scented spiritual energy gathered around them, not rushing directly into Wang Sumei's meridians, but lingering softly around her, easing the oppressive weight the spiritual energy had brought.","\"Grandma, look at me,\" Qin Zhen said softly. \"Breathe in, slow down, then breathe out slowly again.\"","Wang Sumei forced her eyes open, following her granddaughter's voice to adjust her breathing.","One time, two times, three times. The suffocating tightness in her chest finally faded slowly. The soreness and swelling in her meridians were still there, but it was no longer unbearable. After a long while, Wang Sumei finally let out a long, slow breath.","\"Mother, how do you feel?\" Liu Zhen's voice was thick with worry.","Wang Sumei leaned against her daughter-in-law to rest for a moment, then shook her head. \"I'm fine. It was just that first moment when we stepped in, it was really hard to take.\"","She lifted her head and saw the whole family huddled around her, and could not help but smile. \"This old woman has lived such a long life, and I never thought I'd get to step into the Cultivation World one day.\"","Seeing that she was well enough to joke, Qin Wen finally relaxed. \"Mother, you might even get to live over a hundred years from now on.\"","\"Nonsense,\" Wang Sumei shot him a glare. \"I don't know if I'll live that long, but that mouth of yours keeps running, and you'll give your father a fit of anger before I get there.\"","Everyone could not help but laugh, and the previously tense atmosphere melted away. Qin Huai stood to the side, looking at his wife, then at the sons, grandsons and the rest of the family gathered around him. He held the wooden cane that he no longer needed to support his weight, and tapped it lightly once on the ground. \"Everyone made it here safe. Then let's go.\"","Qin Huai turned his gaze toward the deep woods, his voice steady and resolute.","\"Starting today, our Qin family will build our new home right here.\""]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Entering Nanfu City Again","paragraphs":["Several months later, Qin Zhen found herself standing in Nanfeng City once again.","The streets were just as lively as ever. Shops lined both sides of the road, cultivators came and went, and spirit beasts of all shapes and sizes could occasionally be seen passing by. Unlike the first time she had entered the city, Qin Zhen was no longer filled with curiosity. She made her way familiarly through two main streets and stopped in front of the Xiangya Residence.","“Sister Su.”","A familiar voice reached her. Su Qingqing, who was tallying accounts behind the counter, looked up and saw a young girl standing outside, with a burly man behind her. The two shared a few similar features—one glance was enough to tell that they were relatives.","Su Qingqing’s eyes lit up. “Zhenzhen? You’re finally back. I knew it—sooner or later, you’d come to Nanfeng City again.”","Qin Zhen smiled with her lips pressed together. “Sister Su, it’s been a long time.”","“It certainly has.” Su Qingqing looked her up and down, making sure the girl was in good spirits before turning her attention to Qin Wen. “And who is this?”","“My uncle, Qin Wen.”","This was Qin Wen’s first time in a city of the cultivation world, and he was already feeling somewhat awkward. Hearing his niece introduce him, he quickly nodded at Su Qingqing. “Shopkeeper Su.”","Su Qingqing smiled and acknowledged him before looking back at Qin Zhen. “Go on, tell me. You’ve come to see me today for more than just a little catching up, haven’t you?”","Qin Zhen did not beat around the bush. “Sister Su, does the Xiangya Residence buy spirit rice?”","Su Qingqing raised an eyebrow. “Of course.”","She glanced at the handcart behind them, and her smile deepened. “When I saw how well you took care of those azure jade vegetables, I guessed this day would come sooner or later. How much do you have?”","“Two hundred pounds.”","“That much?” Su Qingqing was genuinely surprised this time. “Let me have a look.”","At her words, Qin Wen hurriedly lifted the burlap covering the cart. Beneath it sat several grain sacks arranged in neat rows.","Su Qingqing untied one of the sacks and pinched up a few grains of spirit rice. The grains were crystalline and plump, with a faint luster shimmering across their surfaces. She examined them carefully, then held them beneath her nose and took a light sniff. The surprise in her eyes gradually turned into admiration.","“Not bad, Zhenzhen. Second-grade spirit rice, and the spiritual energy is very pure. The grains are also plumper than most second-grade spirit rice on the market.” Su Qingqing looked up at Qin Zhen. “You grew all of this yourself?”","“Mm. Everyone at home helped grow it.”","“Your skills are already better than those of quite a few proper spirit cultivators in the city.” Su Qingqing tied the sack shut again. “Two hundred pounds. I’ll give you two thousand low-grade spirit stones.”","Qin Zhen had worked at the Xiangya Residence for two months and knew roughly what spirit rice sold for in Nanfeng City. Second-grade spirit rice went for ten low-grade spirit stones per pound, so Su Qingqing’s offer was perfectly fair.","“All right.”","Su Qingqing was just about to take out the spirit stones when Qin Zhen spoke again. “Sister Su, one thousand five hundred will be enough.”","“Hm?” Su Qingqing looked at her.","Qin Zhen said earnestly, “When I went home last time, you gave me fifty spirit stones for the teleportation array. And there were also all those days I spent eating and staying at the Xiangya Residence...”","“Stop, stop, stop.” Su Qingqing raised a finger and gently tapped her on the forehead. “You little girl, why are you still keeping track of that?”","Qin Zhen covered her forehead. “A debt is still a debt.”","“What debt?” Su Qingqing said irritably. “In the two months you spent at the Xiangya Residence, how many spirit vegetables did you save for me? If we were to calculate everything properly, I’m the one who took advantage of you. As for those fifty spirit stones, your sister here isn’t short of such a small amount. Didn’t I say so back then? Consider it an investment in you. In the future, whenever you grow something good, remember to send it to the Xiangya Residence first. That will be your repayment.”","With that, she did not give Qin Zhen any chance to refuse again and directly handed her two thousand low-grade spirit stones.","Qin Zhen held the spirit stones in both hands and fell silent for a moment. In the end, she accepted them. “All right. In the future, if my family has spirit rice or spirit vegetables to sell, I’ll come to you first, Sister Su.”","“That’s more like it.”","Satisfied, Su Qingqing nodded. Qin Zhen carefully put away the spirit stones, then remembered the other reason she had come to the city today.","“Sister Su, do you know where I can buy cultivation techniques?”","“Cultivation techniques?” Su Qingqing was somewhat surprised. “You want to start cultivating?”","Qin Zhen shook her head. “Not me. Someone in my family wants to see whether they can sense spiritual energy and begin cultivating.”","Su Qingqing did not ask any further questions. She merely pointed toward the other end of the street. “Try the Treasure Pavilion. They have just about everything there—pills, magical artifacts, spirit plants, cultivation techniques. As long as you have enough spirit stones, you can buy nearly anything. Of course, the truly good cultivation techniques are mostly controlled by the major sects and cultivation clans. The techniques the Treasure Pavilion sells to the public are generally nothing special.”","Qin Zhen nodded. “Something that can get us started is enough. Thank you, Sister Su.”","“Go on.” Su Qingqing smiled. “And remember to come to me again next time you have spirit rice.”","“I will.”","The uncle and niece said goodbye to Su Qingqing and left the Xiangya Residence, pushing the now-empty handcart. Neither of them noticed the gray-clothed man who had been crouching by the wall across the street slowly raise his head.","His gaze lingered for a moment on the cloth pouch at Qin Zhen’s waist—the one containing her spirit stones—before he casually looked away.","The Treasure Pavilion was not far from the Xiangya Residence. Along the way, Qin Wen’s eyes hardly stopped moving. This was his first time truly entering a city inhabited by cultivators, and everything was new to him: cultivators flying past on swords, pills being sold along the roadside, wooden puppets that could walk on their own, and spirit beasts with all kinds of strange appearances.","“Zhenzhen,” Qin Wen asked in a lowered voice, “was that a multicolored snake crawling on that person’s shoulder?”","“Mm.”","“And what about that one over there? How can that bird speak like a person?”","“Spirit beast.”","“Then...”","“Uncle.” Qin Zhen gave him a helpless look. “If you keep staring, you’re going to walk into someone.”","Qin Wen hurriedly pulled his gaze back. “It’s my first time seeing all this.”","The corners of Qin Zhen’s lips curved faintly. When she had first come to Nanfeng City, she had not been much better than her uncle.","Before long, the two of them arrived at the Treasure Pavilion.","The towering building rose several stories high, and people streamed in and out through its doors. The instant Qin Zhen and Qin Wen stepped inside, they simultaneously felt a faint tremor in their minds.","In the next moment, the scene before them abruptly changed.","Countless jade plaques floated in midair, slowly circling the hall. Each plaque was engraved with different words: pills, spirit plants, spirit pets, magical robes, magical artifacts, formations, talismans...","Qin Wen tilted his head back, his eyes nearly unable to take everything in. “How... how are those things floating up there?”","Qin Zhen was surprised as well. However, during this period, everyone in the Qin family had begun learning the written language of the cultivation world. She quickly found the jade plaque bearing the words “cultivation techniques” among the many others.","She raised her hand and lightly touched the plaque with her fingertip.","A gentle white light rippled outward from the jade plaque. Qin Zhen felt her vision blur. When she could see clearly again, she and Qin Wen were standing in a completely unfamiliar space.","Rows of towering bookshelves stretched into the distance, seemingly without end. Directly before them stood an enormous wall of white jade. At the very top, the characters for metal, wood, water, fire, earth, ice, and lightning were arranged in order. Beneath each attribute were densely packed lists of cultivation techniques.","Qin Wen’s scalp prickled as he stared at them. “There are this many?”","Qin Zhen did not answer. Her gaze landed on the far left side of the jade wall, where no attributes were marked, only a few simple characters were written.","Introductory Basic Cultivation Technique. Qin Zhen walked over and reached out to touch it, and a line of text slowly surfaced on the jade wall.","*Qi ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Introduction to the Body Formula*, a non-attribute basic cultivation technique, can be used to sense the spiritual energy of heaven and earth, guide spiritual energy into the body, and is suitable for people who are new to cultivation. Price: 500 low-grade spirit stones.","\"Five hundred?\" Qin Wen gasped, \"Niece, you worked hard planting spiritual rice for several months and only sold it for two thousand spirit stones. Just this one introductory technique costs five hundred?\"","Qin Zhen also thought it was expensive, but right now, none of them even knew which member of the family had a spiritual root, or what attribute cultivation technique they should practice. This *Qi Introduction to the Body Formula* was the most suitable one at the very least, it could let the family members try to sense spiritual energy first.","She did not hesitate for long. Her finger gently tapped on the name of *Qi Introduction to the Body Formula*, and a small white jade tray extended out from under the jade wall. Qin Zhen counted out five hundred low-grade spirit stones and placed them on the tray. The moment the spirit stones landed, they were covered by a white light. In the next instant, all the spirit stones vanished, and a pale cyan jade slip slowly appeared in the center of the tray.","Qin Zhen picked up the jade slip and handed it to Qin Wen, \"Uncle, keep this safe.\"","\"Me?\" Qin Wen quickly stretched out both hands to catch it.","The jade slip felt cool and smooth in his hand. He flipped it over and over several times, handling it with extreme care. Five hundred spirit stones, he had never touched something this expensive in his entire life.","\"Don't worry, even if I fall myself, I won't let this thing drop.\"","She did not respond, and continued to look through the cultivation techniques on the jade wall.","Gold, Wood, Water, Fire, Earth...","Qin Zhen looked extremely carefully. She wanted to find a cultivation method that matched her own situation: no spiritual root, yet able to sense plants and trees, promote the growth of spiritual plants, and borrow the spiritual energy from inside the spiritual plants. But after going through all the cultivation techniques she could find, she did not discover any description similar to her situation. After staring for a long time, Qin Zhen felt dizzy and could only give up temporarily.","Just as she was about to leave, she suddenly spotted the words \"Spiritual Plants\" on another jade plaque, and her footsteps immediately halted. A moment later, a jade slip titled *The Complete Book of Spiritual Plant Cultivation* was in her hand.","Price: 1,200 low-grade spirit stones.","Seeing the price, the corners of Qin Wen's mouth twitched, \"Zhenzhen...\"","\"We're buying it!\"","Qin Zhen did not hesitate. She could not find a suitable cultivation technique for the time being, but growing spiritual plants was the fundamental way for the Qin family to settle down and make a living in the cultivation world. Although she could sense spiritual plants, she barely knew anything about the types, habits, and uses of the spiritual plants in the cultivation world. This book was far more important to her than a cultivation technique that she could not practice for the time being.","Another 1,200 low-grade spirit stones vanished, and an extra jade slip appeared in Qin Zhen's hand.","Two thousand spirit stones were spent in the blink of an eye, leaving only three hundred left. Qin Wen ached so much at the sight that his heart hurt, but Qin Zhen remained very calm. Spirit stones could be earned again. As long as they could still grow spiritual rice, they would never run out of ways to earn spirit stones.","The two of them did not stay any longer and soon left the Treasure Gather Studio. However, just after walking down one street, Qin Zhen's pace slowed down imperceptibly.","She could not tell if it was an illusion, but ever since she left Treasure Gather Studio, she had the constant feeling that someone was behind them. The feeling was not obvious, there were no footsteps, and no one was staring at her the whole time, but she just felt uncomfortable, just like when she was walking in the mountains and being watched by some wild beast hiding in the dark.","Qin Zhen did not turn her head. \"Uncle, let's take a different route.\"","Qin Wen was still feeling distressed over the 1,700 spirit stones.","\"Huh?\"","Qin Zhen had already turned into the street beside them. Though confused, Qin Wen still pushed the cart to follow her. \"Why are we going this way all of a sudden?\"","\"I want to rent a spirit beast.\"","\"Rent a spirit beast?\" Qin Wen was stunned. \"Weren't we going to walk back?\"","\"It's too slow,\" Qin Zhen said in a calm tone. \"The family is waiting for the cultivation technique. We should get back earlier.\"","She did not mention that she felt someone was following them. Cultivators had sharp senses, she did not know where the other party was, nor if the person was a cultivator. If she rashly warned her uncle, it might alert the stalker instead.","Luckily, Qin Zhen had lived in Nanfu City for a period of time before, so she knew there was a place in the city that specialized in renting out riding spirit beasts. For short-distance travels, people could rent tamed spirit beasts. After reaching the destination, they only needed to untie the return tether on the spirit beast, and the beast would automatically make its way back to its owner.","Qin Zhen led Qin Wen through several consecutive streets, and finally walked into a spirit beast shop.","\"We're leaving the cart here.\"","Qin Wen was stunned. \"Leave it behind?\"","\"Yes.\" Qin Zhen glanced outside. \"That old wooden cart isn't worth much. We can make a new one later.\"","Though Qin Wen was reluctant to part with it, he did not object. Before long, the uncle and niece were standing in front of a giant rabbit that stood half as tall as a person. Qin Wen craned his neck to look up at it, and the rabbit lowered its head to look back at Qin Wen. The human and the rabbit stared at each other, wide-eyed.","\"Zhenzhen... This thing... Can we really ride it?\"","\"It should be able to.\"","\"It won't throw us off, right?\"","Qin Zhen was silent for a moment. \"It probably won't.\"","Actually, it was her first time riding one too. A wide, woven rattan seat basket was fixed to the giant rabbit's back, spacious enough for two people. Qin Wen climbed into it trembling with fear, and Qin Zhen also sat down, putting on a calm front.","The clerk at the spirit beast shop untied the reins and gave the giant rabbit's rump a light pat. The next moment, the giant rabbit suddenly bolted off.","\"AHHH!\"","Qin Wen's scream vanished instantly as they shot down the end of the street. Qin Zhen gripped the edge of the rattan basket tightly, realizing that she had been too optimistic earlier. This was not just a little bumpy. Every time the giant rabbit landed, she felt like her internal organs were bouncing along with it.","Qin Wen was even paler, his hands clutching the rattan basket for dear life. \"N-niece...\"","\"Next time...\"","\"Let's just walk...\"","Qin Zhen did not answer, because she was about to throw up too. Cultivators could use their spiritual energy to protect their bodies, so they would not fear this kind of bumpiness, but the uncle and niece were both mortals right now, so they could only endure the whole jolting ride.","As uncomfortable as it was, the giant rabbit's speed was extremely fast. In just the time it takes to burn a few sticks of incense, Nanfu City had been left far behind. Meanwhile, on a side road outside the city, two gray-robed men stopped in their tracks.","\"Where did they go?\"","\"They were right in front of us a moment ago.\"","One of the men looked ugly. The other closed his eyes to sense for a moment, then looked into the distance, where only a tiny, shrinking shadow could be seen.","\"They rented a spirit beast. We can't catch up now.\"","\"Lucky bastards.\"","The man's face was dark. They had initially seen two mortals coming out of the Fragrant Elegance Pavilion, and had watched them enter Treasure Gather Studio with their own eyes. Two mortals, no spiritual energy, carrying at least a thousand low-grade spirit stones on them.","This kind of fat sheep was rarely seen outside Nanfu City. As long as they waited for the two to leave the city, no one would ever know what had happened. But who could have guessed that two mortals who looked so stingy that they would hate to part with a single spirit stone would suddenly rent a spirit beast to hurry on their way.","\"Let's go. It's not worth chasing them just for a few hundred spirit stones.\"","The figures of the two quickly vanished along the mountain path. On the other side, the giant hare had been dashing nonstop the entire way, and finally skidded to a halt at the outer edge of the mountain forest. No matter how much Qin Zhen urged it, it refused to take another step forward.","There were no roads commonly used by cultivators ahead, only dense ancient trees and tangled vines. The giant hare held its ears high upright, its front paws scraping frantically at the ground, clearly extremely resistant to venturing deep into the forest.","Left with no choice, Qin Zhen and Qin Wen climbed down from the carrying basket. The moment Qin Wen's feet touched solid ground, his whole body swayed. He grabbed hold of a nearby tree and said, \"Give me a second to catch my breath... I swear my soul is still chasing after us from back there.\"","Qin Zhen wasn't faring much better herself. She leaned against a tree trunk for a while before untying the return tether fastened to the giant hare.","The instant the knot came undone, the giant hare looked as if it had been granted the greatest pardon imaginable. It spun around and bolted, vanishing without a trace in the blink of an eye.","Qin Wen stared at the direction it had disappeared in for a long moment in silence, then said, \"It ran that fast? It almost makes it look like it couldn't stand the thought of escorting us any further, doesn't it?\"","\"Probably,\" Qin Zhen replied.","She turned to face the deep expanse of the forest. That vague, lingering unease that had been tugging at her heart the entire way had faded away at some point. She did not mention it to her uncle, only tightened her grip on the cloth pouch holding the two jade slips. \"Let's go. The family is waiting for us to get back.\"","The uncle and his niece soon disappeared into the trees.","They had no idea that just moments earlier, that inexplicable flicker of unease that had risen in Qin Zhen's heart had already let them dodge the first real deadly trap they had encountered since stepping into the cultivation world."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Drawing Qi into the Body","paragraphs":["Several more days passed before Qin Zhen and Qin Wen finally returned home. The moment the Qin family spotted them in the distance, the anxiety they had been carrying at last eased.","“They’re back!”","Liu Zhen was the first to rush forward. She looked her daughter over from head to toe, and only after confirming that she was safe and unharmed did she truly let out a breath of relief.","Qin Ye patted his younger brother on the shoulder as well.","“Why were you gone so long?”","That question immediately opened the floodgates for Qin Wen.","“You have no idea—the cultivators in Nanfu City are practically no different from the immortals in storybooks!”","“Some of them were standing on swords and flying through the sky! And at the Treasure Pavilion, all the jade slips were floating in midair!”","“Oh, and there was this colorful snake—I saw it with my own eyes!”","“And that rabbit we rode on when we came back—it was huge...”","Standing to one side, Qin Zhen silently watched her uncle for a moment.","So this was what happened to everyone the first time they entered the world of cultivation?","He looked... a little foolish. And rather noisy.","Then she remembered that when she had first entered Nanfu City, she too had stared at this and gawked at that. When she returned, she had probably talked nonstop as well.","Qin Zhen quietly looked away.","Better not think too deeply about that sort of thing.","“Grandfather, Grandmother.”","She simply cut Qin Wen off.","“Father, Mother, Uncle—the cultivation manual has been bought.”","The moment those words fell, the lively courtyard went silent.","Even Qin Wen shut his mouth. Qin Zhen took a pale green jade slip from her bundle.","“We can begin trying to draw spiritual energy into our bodies.”","The Qin family stared at the small jade slip, their expressions complicated—anticipation, nervousness, and a trace of unspoken unease.","Having come to the world of cultivation, it was impossible for them not to want to cultivate. Though they had once been ordinary mortals, after seeing cultivators fly on swords with their own eyes and experiencing the wonders of this world firsthand, how could they have no such aspirations at all?","Yet the greater their hopes, the greater their fear. They feared they would be unable to sense spiritual energy at all. They feared they possessed no spiritual roots. They feared that, after struggling so hard to come here, they would ultimately remain nothing more than ordinary mortals.","After a moment of silence, Qin Huai looked at Qin Zhen.","“Zhenzhen, you try first.”","“Although Master Chen said you have no spiritual roots, among everyone in this family, you are actually the one most likely to succeed in cultivating. You could already sense spiritual plants, and you can already draw upon spiritual energy. Let’s see whether this cultivation method works for you.”","Qin Zhen hesitated briefly before nodding.","“All right.”","She sat down cross-legged and followed the method she had seen at the Treasure Pavilion, pressing the jade slip to her forehead.","The next instant—","Boom!","A vast quantity of text surged into her mind.","Qin Zhen felt her head grow heavy, as though someone had forcibly crammed an entire book into her memories.","The contents of the *Art of Drawing Qi into the Body* appeared clearly, word by word: beginning with how to calm the mind and sense spiritual energy, then how to guide it, and finally how to circulate it through the meridians once it entered the body.","Before she could recover, the jade slip in her hand gave a faint crack.","Crack!","In the next moment, it shattered directly into a handful of fine white powder.","“Ah!”","Qin Wen jumped in fright.","“How did it shatter? That was worth five hundred spirit stones!”","Qin Zhen lowered her head to look at the powder in her hand, then sensed the contents now residing in her mind.","“It’s fine. The cultivation method is all in my head. It’s just... if I can still recite it after learning it, why did the jade slip have to break?”","Liu Zhen could not help laughing. Reaching out, she stroked her daughter’s head.","“Broken is broken. Try it first. As long as it works, that’s what matters.”","“Mm.”","Qin Zhen closed her eyes and followed the first step of the *Art of Drawing Qi into the Body*: first, she had to still her mind.","For ordinary people, sensing the spiritual energy between heaven and earth was perhaps the hardest part.","Yet the moment Qin Zhen calmed herself, she sensed the familiar presences around her.","In the past, she had only been vaguely aware of spiritual energy, especially near spirit plants, where the sensation was much clearer. But she had never known how to truly draw that energy into her body. Most of the time, she could only rely on her connection with the spirit plants to stir the spiritual energy already within them.","Until now.","The cultivation method had finally opened a door for her. Qin Zhen slowed her breathing and, following the incantation, cautiously guided the surrounding spiritual energy toward herself.","At first, the spiritual energy merely circled around her, unwilling to draw near. She did not rush.","Once.","Twice.","Three times.","Gradually, a wisp of exceedingly faint spiritual energy entered her body with her breath. Qin Zhen’s heart stirred.","She did not try to seize it. Instead, as the method instructed, she guided that thread of spiritual energy slowly into her meridians. The instant it entered her body, it brought a faint chill. Carefully, she urged it onward, passing through one meridian after another.","At the beginning, that wisp of spiritual energy was so thin that it was almost imperceptible. Yet as it circulated, it gradually became stable.","Qin Zhen became completely immersed in the process. By the time she had completed a full minor circulation according to the method and opened her eyes again, the sky had already darkened.","She froze for a moment. Had so much time really passed?","Before she could carefully sense the changes in her body, she looked up—and saw five people standing neatly before her, five pairs of eyes staring at her without blinking.","Qin Zhen’s heart gave a violent leap.","“Have you... been waiting a long time?”","Qin Wen was crouched at the very front.","“No.”","Qin Zhen silently gave him a look. Then she carefully sensed the inside of her body. Sure enough, a wisp of extremely faint spiritual energy remained in her meridians. It was not much, but it was real.","“I think...”","Qin Zhen hesitated.","“I succeeded?”","Liu Zhen immediately broke into a smile.","“My Zhenzhen is so amazing. Of course you succeeded.”","“Mom...”","“All right, all right.” Liu Zhen waved her hand with a grin. “I won’t say any more. You’re getting embarrassed.”","Qin Zhen’s ears grew slightly warm. She simply turned her attention back to the cultivation method.","“I’ll recite the *Art of Drawing Qi into the Body* now. Everyone, try to memorize it. If you can’t remember it all at once, I’ll repeat it as many times as needed.”","The Qin family immediately became serious. Qin Zhen then recited the cultivation method from beginning to end.","The first time, everyone looked bewildered. The second time, they seemed to have remembered some of it. By the third time, Qin Wen had started scratching his head. By the fourth, Wang Sumei was already quietly repeating the incantation under her breath.","By the fifth time... even Qin Zhen was nearly numb from reciting it. Only then did the family barely manage to memorize the contents. Afterward, everyone found a place to try cultivating on their own, and the house fell so quiet that one could hear a pin drop.","Qin Zhen did not disturb them. She rose and headed for the spirit fields her parents had newly reclaimed during the past few days while she had been away.","Another batch of spirit rice had already been planted. As Qin Zhen stepped into the field, her footsteps suddenly paused.","Perhaps because she had successfully drawn qi into her body, her perception of her surroundings seemed to have become sharper. The emotions radiating from each young spirit-rice shoot were far more distinct than before.","Joy. Ease. A longing for water and sunlight. Even the spiritual energy in the air felt more tangible to her than it had before.","Qin Zhen clenched her fist. Her body seemed lighter as well. Though she had been busy all day, she did not feel sleepy in the slightest. Instead, it was as if she were brimming with inexhaustible energy.","Looking down at the spirit field before her, she knew that if the entire family could cultivate in the future, they would only need more and more spirit stones.","Cultivation manuals, pills, magical artifacts, cultivation resources—what among them did not cost spirit stones?","Even the most basic *Qi Drawing Technique* cost five hundred low-grade spirit stones. At that thought, Qin Zhen silently picked up her hoe.","They still had to farm—and they had to farm even more.","Her ability to sense plants’ emotions was her greatest asset. As long as she could make good use of it, the Qin family would at least never lack a way to earn spirit stones.","Qin Zhen worked the field for a while before a thought suddenly occurred to her.","Whenever she cultivated near spiritual plants, she always felt more comfortable...","Did that mean she could absorb spiritual energy faster in the spirit fields?","She set her hoe aside and sat cross-legged directly on the ridge between the fields.","Closing her eyes, she began circulating her cultivation technique.","Sure enough, once the *Qi Drawing Technique* began to circulate again, the spiritual energy around her seemed to gather a little faster.","The change was not obvious, but Qin Zhen could feel it.","In particular, the spiritual energy around the young spirit-rice shoots beside her was noticeably more active.","She circulated her qi through one cycle after another, and before she knew it, dawn had come again.","Qin Zhen slowly opened her eyes. The morning mist in the mountains had yet to fully disperse, but she froze.","She could see the dewdrops on distant branches more clearly than before. She could even make out the direction in which blades of grass not far away swayed gently in the breeze.","She tried taking a breath. The scent of earth, the fragrance of grass, the dampness in the air—all of it seemed clearer than before.","The changes were slight, but they were real.","Qin Zhen could not help lowering her head to look at her hands.","So this was what changed after drawing qi into the body.","Not long afterward, the other members of the Qin family emerged from the house one after another. Every one of them wore a rather stiff expression. Qin Zhen glanced around; there was no need to ask. No one had succeeded.","Qin Wen plopped down onto the ridge between the fields.","“I sat there all night until my legs went numb. Never mind spiritual energy—I couldn’t even catch hold of the wind.”","Wang Sumei let out a sigh. Though Qin Ye said nothing, a trace of disappointment inevitably showed on his face.","Seeing this, Qin Zhen quickly spoke up.","“It’s ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍all right.”","Everyone turned to look at her.","“If we can’t do it in one day, then we’ll keep trying for a few more. We all came from the mortal world—how could we possibly receive cultivation techniques and master qi absorption in a single night?”","She pointed to herself.","“I’ve always been able to sense spiritual plants, and I’ve been around spiritual qi all this time. It’s only natural that I’d be a little faster.”","“If everyone could become a cultivator after one night of practice, wouldn’t the mortal world be full of cultivators already?”","Thinking it over, everyone realized that she was right. Qin Wen rubbed his nose.","“True. If I really became an immortal after just one night, I’d be wondering whether I was dreaming.”","The somewhat dispirited mood immediately lifted. Since they could not learn it all at once, life still had to go on.","So the Qin family quickly became busy again. When they grew tired of cultivating, they cleared land. When clearing land tired them out, they meditated. When they were hungry, they ate; when sleepy, they took a nap.","After some time, even their sleeping place gradually shifted from the wooden cabin to beside the spirit fields. The reason was simple: Qin Zhen had discovered that cultivating near spiritual plants seemed to allow one to absorb spiritual qi a little faster. The moment she said so, the Qin family carried their straw mats over the very next day.","Later, they even moved their cooking pot to the edge of the fields. A crude little shelter was put up beside the spirit fields; they farmed during the day and cultivated at night.","The entire family revolved around the spirit fields every day. Sometimes, several days would pass without everyone managing to sit down for even a single meal together. Just like that, the Qin family truly made their home in the fields.","Day by day, the amount of spiritual qi Qin Zhen could store within her body grew greater, while the others continued trying without pause.","Then, one day, Qin Zhen was weeding the spirit rice when hurried footsteps suddenly sounded behind her.","“Zhenzhen!”","Qin Zhen turned around. Liu Zhen was hurrying toward her, her usually gentle and composed face now filled with unconcealed joy.","“Mother?”","Qin Zhen set down the hoe in her hand. Liu Zhen came up to her, her voice trembling slightly.","“Zhenzhen, I think I succeeded.”","Qin Zhen’s eyes instantly lit up.","“Really?”","“Mother, tell me what it felt like.”","Liu Zhen closed her eyes and carefully recalled what had happened the night before.","“Before, whenever I closed my eyes, I could faintly sense a kind of very pleasant energy around me. But no matter how I tried to guide it according to the cultivation technique, it wouldn’t enter my body. The more I tried to grasp it, the more it scattered.”","She spoke slowly.","“But yesterday was different. Yesterday, as I sat beside the spirit fields, I suddenly felt that energy was especially close to me.”","“And then...”","Liu Zhen paused.","“It was like a door that had been shut suddenly opened, and that energy rushed into my body. I didn’t dare move. I could only follow the cultivation technique you taught me and guide it along, little by little.”","“From here...”","She pointed to her chest.","“Then to my arms, then to my legs... and finally, after making a full circuit, it returned to where it began.”","Liu Zhen opened her eyes, unable to suppress the smile on her face any longer.","“After it completed the circuit, I felt completely different—as though every limb and every bone in my body had opened up.”","Qin Zhen froze for a moment, then broke into a broad smile.","“Mother.”","“You succeeded.”","“Really?”","Qin Zhen nodded emphatically.","“Congratulations, Mother. You’ve successfully drawn spiritual energy into your body.”","Liu Zhen’s eyes immediately reddened. She lowered her head and looked at her hands.","She really... could cultivate too?","Not far away, Qin Ye, Qin Wen, Qin Huai, and Wang Sumei had clearly overheard the exchange between mother and daughter. They all gathered around.","“My daughter-in-law really succeeded?”","“Sister-in-law, you truly sensed spiritual energy?”","“Tell us quickly—what did it feel like?”","For a time, the fields became incredibly lively. Although Qin Ye had yet to succeed himself, he was happier than anyone.","“Good!”","“If one person can do it, that proves this path works!”","Qin Wen nodded vigorously as well.","“If Sister-in-law has succeeded, then I’ll keep trying for a few more days. I can’t fall too far behind her.”","Liu Zhen did not know whether to laugh or cry.","“You can turn cultivation into a competition?”","“Why not?” Qin Wen replied as if it were only natural.","Everyone burst into laughter. Standing among them, Qin Zhen watched her mother laugh so happily, and an unprecedented sense of peace settled in her heart.","Her younger sister, Qin Jia, had long since embarked on the immortal path, and Qin Zhen herself had finally completed the crucial step of drawing spiritual energy into her body.","And now—","Her mother had succeeded as well. Their family finally had a third person who had truly set foot upon the path of cultivation.","It also meant that their decision to move into the world of cultivators had not been wrong.","The Qin family’s road to immortality had truly begun."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Harvest","paragraphs":["Several months had slipped by before anyone realized it. Over these past months, the family’s life had barely changed at all. They cultivated their spiritual arts, tended to the fields, ate their meals, then went right back to cultivating again—days so busy that time flowed past almost unnoticed.","The good news was that after Liu Zhen, Qin Wen and Qin Ye had also successfully drawn their first wisp of spiritual energy into their bodies one after another. None of the three moved particularly fast in their cultivation, and they did not even know yet what type of spiritual roots they possessed. But the very fact that they could guide spiritual energy into their bodies meant they had crossed the first threshold separating ordinary mortals from cultivators.","Now, out of the seven members of the Qin family, only Qin Huai and Wang Sumei had not yet succeeded. The two elders were not discouraged in the slightest; if anything, they felt even more at peace than when they first started. The facts had already proven that the Qin family had not made the wrong choice when they moved to the cultivation realm. At the very least, their sons and daughter-in-law truly could practice cultivation.","As for themselves, succeeding at it would be wonderful, but even if they did not, staying by their children’s sides and watching the Qin family slowly take root in this land was more than enough for them.","One early morning, Qin Zhen stood at the edge of the fields, looking out at the spirit rice that had already heavy, drooping heads of grain. Vast stretches of rice swayed gently in the morning breeze. Compared to when they had first sown the seeds, the spirit fields now looked completely transformed. Each stalk of spirit rice was plump and sturdy, a faint glow of spiritual light clinging to the surface of the grains, and the air was thick with the sweet, fresh scent of rice.","Qin Zhen squatted down and reached out to brush one of the stalks. The spirit rice’s leaves swayed softly near her fingertips, conveying a sense of joy, contentment, and the giddy eagerness of something fully ripe, impatient to be harvested.","Qin Zhen’s eyes crinkled into a smile. “Mom, they’re ready to harvest!”","The moment she finished speaking, movement came from the small shed nearby. Liu Zhen opened her eyes, pulling herself out of her meditative cultivation state. “They’re really ripe?”","She stood up and grabbed the long sword set beside her. That sword had been brought back by Qin Jia when she first came home. No one in the Qin family had been able to wield it back then, so Qin Zhen had only ever managed to nudge it into motion using the spiritual energy from spirit plants. Now that Liu Zhen had successfully drawn spiritual energy into her body, the sword finally had a new purpose.","She did not know any formal sword techniques, but channeling a small amount of spiritual energy into the blade was more than enough to cut down the spirit rice. Liu Zhen held the sword, looking out over the golden expanse of the spirit fields, a smile spreading across her face.","Back then, she could only follow behind her daughter to help out—carrying things, hauling water, pulling weeds. Most of the time, she could only stand by and watch Qin Zhen do all the hard work. Now, she could finally lend her daughter a real hand.","“Everyone, stop your cultivation! The spirit rice is ripe!” Liu Zhen called toward the house. It was not long before all the Qin family members emerged from wherever they had been.","“Ripe already?” Qin Wen did not even get his shoes on properly before hurrying over to the field edge. “That fast?”","Qin Ye had already rolled up his sleeves. “Hardly fast, it’s been months. Stop standing there staring, let’s get to work.”","Qin Huai and Wang Sumei walked over carrying the bamboo baskets they had prepared, and the whole family quickly got to work. Liu Zhen, Qin Ye, and Qin Wen handled the harvesting, while Qin Zhen checked how ripe each patch of spirit rice was and organized the cut bundles of grain. Qin Huai and Wang Sumei tied the bundles up and carried them back.","With the whole family working together, the large stretch of spirit fields was mostly harvested in no time. What surprised all of them the most was that after working for so long, none of them felt the aching, drained exhaustion they would have collapsed under in the old days.","When the last bundle of spirit rice had been carried back, Qin Ye stood on the ridge between the fields and stretched his shoulders. “Everything’s different.”","Qin Wen was tipping spirit rice into a bamboo basket, and he looked up at that. “What’s different?”","“My body.” Qin Ye patted his own arm. “Back then, harvesting a field this big would have left me needing to rest for half a day. Now I don’t feel tired at all.”","Qin Wen realized he was right, and he unconsciously clenched his fist. “You’re not kidding. No wonder everyone wants to cultivate immortality. Forget flying through the sky and tunneling through the earth—just having a body this strong is already so much better than what we had before.”","Liu Zhen laughed from beside them. “You’ve only just drawn spiritual energy into your body, and you’re already spouting that kind of talk?”","“Still counts as cultivating immortality, doesn’t it?” Qin Wen said, unapologetic.","Qin Ye gave his brother a look of playful disdain. “You can talk about that after you finish packing up all this spirit rice.”","Qin Zhen listened to her family chatting back and forth casually, and the corners of her mouth lifted into a smile.","This kind of life was really nice. No one was chasing them, no one was pressuring them. The whole family lived in peace, tending the fields and practicing cultivation. When the spirit rice ripened, they harvested it together, and once Jiajia came out of her seclusion, they would find a way to get in touch with her. The tight, anxious knot in Qin Zhen’s chest had slowly unspooled and steadied over these past few months.","Once all the spirit rice was properly stored away, the whole family sat down together. Qin Zhen thought for a moment before speaking. “We need to go into town again.”","Qin Huai looked up. “Did we run out of something?”","“So many things.” Qin Zhen started counting off on her fingers. “Dad, Mom, and Uncle Qin all successfully drew spiritual energy into their bodies now, but we still don’t know what kind of spiritual roots each of them has. We can only figure out what cultivation methods to buy once we test their spiritual roots—we can’t keep using the most basic *Spirit Drawing Art* forever.”","She glanced over at the newly harvested spirit rice as she spoke. “Then there’s seeds. Right now we only have these few types of spirit plants. If we want to make spirit stones growing spirit plants in the future, we can’t just keep planting spirit rice forever. And farm tools. Ordinary iron tools work for now, but the *Complete Guide to Spirit Plant Cultivation* says some spirit fields and spirit plants can’t be handled with ordinary iron tools.”","She paused at that. “And there’s pests.”","Wang Sumei blinked in surprise. “Pests?”","“Right.” Qin Zhen nodded. “The *Complete Guide to Spirit Plant Cultivation* writes all about them. Spirit-eating bugs, root-boring bugs, and bugs that specifically chew through spirit plant leaves. Some of these pests can devour an entire large spirit field overnight. There’s also the spirit-sucking vine I ran into at the Elegant Fragrance Inn before—all of those things can destroy our spirit fields.”","Qin Wen unconsciously glanced back toward their fields. “How come we never ran into any of that?”","Qin Zhen went quiet for a second. That was something that had always struck her as odd.","The book made it very clear that the biggest troubles with spirit fields, besides the soil, spiritual energy, and water supply, were pests. Especially when you opened up a spirit field out in the wild, you were far more likely to draw all kinds of bugs and pests. But they had been planting for months now—they had not run into a single bad pest, not even regular bugs that nibble on leaves.","Qin Zhen had not thought much of it before, but now that she was looking back, something felt off.","“I don’t know. Maybe the environment in this mountain forest is special. But just because we haven’t had pests yet doesn’t mean we never will. We’d better buy some things to keep pests away when we go to town this time.”","Qin Huai nodded. “We should get everything we need to be prepared.”","“There’s one more thing.” Qin Zhen gently touched the concentric pendant hanging at her chest. “We should also ask around for news about Jiajia. It’s been months now, we don’t know if she’s finished her seclusion yet.”","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍the mention of Qin Jia, the whole family fell quiet for a moment. A flash of longing crossed Liu Zhen’s face. “You’re right, we should ask. Even if she’s still in seclusion, it would be good just to know she’s safe.”","Qin Huai thought for a moment, then suddenly looked over at Qin Zhen. “Zhenzhen, have you ever thought about going to Qingyun Sect?”","Qin Huai looked at her, his expression earnest. \"Jiajia is at Qingyun Sect right now. Since you've also awakened the ability to cultivate, why not give it a try? If you can get into the sect, you'll have proper masters guiding your practice, which is far better than fumbling around all on your own like you are now. You'll also get to keep Jiajia company. You're still so young, and Grandfather was worried that if we left you stuck here, we'd only end up holding you back.\"","Liu Zhen did not speak, but the look she gave her daughter clearly showed she shared that very same concern.","Qin Zhen, however, did not hesitate for long. \"No, not right now at least.\"","\"Master Chen personally tested me before and confirmed I have no spiritual root, but here I am able to cultivate anyway. That fact alone is highly unusual.\"","Qin Zhen's voice was steady and calm. \"I spent a few months in Nanfu City, and even though the cultivation world is full of immortal feats, it's far from safer than the mortal realm. On the contrary, with cultivators wielding immense power, many things are far more dangerous than anything you'd see in the secular world. Killing others to seize their treasures is hardly a rare occurrence there.\"","The look of expectation on Liu Zhen's face slowly faded, replaced by deep worry.","Qin Zhen continued, \"If word got out about my strange situation, I have no idea what kind of trouble that would bring. Qingyun Sect is a great and powerful sect, but I don't even know why I can cultivate without a spiritual root in the first place. Rushing over there now would be far too dangerous. At the very least, we need to wait for Jiajia to leave her seclusion, get in touch with her, and ask for her opinion before we decide on our next step.\"","Qin Huai fell silent for a long moment before heaving a soft sigh. \"You're right to think things through so carefully.\"","He had only been worried about holding his granddaughter back, but he understood full well what Qin Zhen had said. The cultivation world was no charitable place. News of someone with no spiritual root who could still cultivate would spread fast, and no one could tell if it would bring great fortune or unthinkable disaster.","\"Alright, as long as you know what you're doing. For now, we can grow spirit plants and earn spirit stones, so let's just keep living our lives in peace.\"","Wang Sumei nodded in agreement. \"There's no rush. We'll take things one step at a time.\"","The whole family quickly decided who would make the trip to the city. Qin Ye, Liu Zhen, and Qin Wen all needed to go to get their spiritual roots tested, and Qin Zhen would naturally travel with them too. Qin Huai and Wang Sumei would stay behind to watch over the spirit fields and the newly harvested spirit rice.","The next day, the family packed up the spirit rice they planned to sell and the food they would need for the road, then set off once again.","After successfully drawing in their first wisp of qi to enter the initial stage of cultivation, Qin Ye and the other two had far better stamina than before. The stretches of road that used to require them to stop and rest for ages could now be traveled nonstop day and night without them feeling overly exhausted.","Qin Zhen's changes were even more pronounced. She felt as long as there was spiritual energy flowing through her body, she had endless strength to spare.","The journey went perfectly smoothly, until the fourth night.","Moonlight filtered through the gaps in the tree canopies, casting a hazy glow over the mountain path. Qin Ye pushed the wooden cart, and when he noticed his daughter had not come up to rest for a while, he spoke up. \"Zhenzhen, hop on the cart and get some sleep. I'll push you along.\"","Qin Zhen shook her head. \"Father, I'm not tired.\"","\"You've been walking the entire day,\" Liu Zhen added. \"Even if you aren't tired, you still need to rest a little.\"","Qin Zhen did not reply. Instead, she furrowed her brows slightly and scanned her surroundings.","At some point, a vague sense of unease had crept into her chest. It was not the sharp, targeted feeling of being watched that she had experienced when someone tailed her before. This was stranger, like something was calling to her, far away yet somehow close at the same time.","Qin Zhen stopped in her tracks without thinking.","\"Zhenzhen?\" Qin Wen turned back to look at her. \"What's wrong?\"","Qin Zhen did not answer. She only stared into the forest on the right side of the road, where ancient trees grew so densely that almost no moonlight could pierce through the foliage, leaving nothing but a deep, dark shadow visible.","Yet she had this inexplicable feeling that something in there was waiting for her.","\"Did any of you hear a sound?\"","The whole group fell quiet at once. The mountain wind blew, rustling the leaves, and a few crickets chirped in the distance. There was nothing else to be heard.","Qin Ye frowned. \"No, what did you hear?\"","Qin Zhen hesitated for a moment. \"I'm not sure.\"","She had not actually heard a sound with her ears. That feeling was only growing stronger, though — it was as if countless plants and trees were sending her some kind of emotion, urgent, longing, and laced with a faint trace of sorrow.","Qin Zhen's chest tightened all of a sudden, and she looked up at the trees nearby.","Normally, whenever she took the initiative to reach out with her senses, all these plants would respond to her. But right now, every single tree around her was eerily silent. She could not even pick up the most basic, ordinary emotions they usually gave off.","They were all waiting.","Qin Zhen unconsciously took a step forward.","\"Zhenzhen.\" Liu Zhen grabbed her wrist at once. \"Where are you going?\"","Qin Zhen snapped back to her senses. \"Mother... it feels like someone over there is calling me.\"","The faces of the Qin family members all paled. Qin Ye immediately stepped in front of her, blocking her path. \"We're not going over there. Let's leave now.\"","There were all kinds of bizarre, unknowable things in the cultivation world. Whatever this thing was, calling for his daughter in the middle of the night in the deep mountains, there was no way it meant well.","Qin Zhen agreed with her father. She forced herself to tear her gaze away. \"Right, let's go.\"","But the second she turned around, a gust of wind swept through the forest. Thousands upon thousands of leaves trembled at the same time, their rustling merging into one continuous roar.","Qin Zhen's feet froze mid-step.","This time, she understood. It was not a sound at all, but an extremely ancient, feeble thought.","Come...","Qin Zhen's pupils widened. The next instant, a ring of pale green light lit up on the ground right under her feet.","\"Zhenzhen!\"","Liu Zhen's face went deathly pale. She lunged out to grab her, and Qin Zhen instinctively reached back for her mother. But before their fingers could touch, the scene all around Qin Zhen twisted sharply. Everything blurred as if seen through a rippling curtain of water.","Qin Zhen did not even have time to speak before the world went completely dark in front of her eyes.","When she opened them again, everything around her had changed entirely.","Qin Zhen was standing in the middle of a deathly quiet ancient forest. Every tree here was towering to an unimaginable height. Their thick trunks would take several people linking arms to wrap around, their canopies blocking out the sky and sun, and the ground was carpeted with all kinds of plants she had never seen before in her life.","And at the very center of this ancient forest stood a single tree.","Qin Zhen lifted her head, but for a moment, she could not even see its crown.","This tree was simply enormous. Its gnarled, sprawling roots coiled across the entire valley, seeming to merge as one with the earth beneath. Its bark was crisscrossed with cracks left by untold years of time, and some parts had long since turned dead and withered. Yet between those fissures, a faint, soft green light flowed slowly.","Standing before it, Qin Zhen felt for the first time a clear, powerful emotion that no ordinary plant could ever give off. It was exhaustion, decay, and yet a gentle warmth that had been tempered by eons of time.","Right after that, that ancient, hoary thought echoed once more in the depths of her mind. It was not a human voice, yet its meaning was perfectly clear to her.","At last...","I've been waiting for you."]}]);
